{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824555251,"sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9db5746001djukcE2UM4Honj","sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","messageID":"msg_0b9db4e980018e5LySXUwMVTqS","type":"tool","id":"call_00_XWKM66gL0L2WONdjUcjG3469","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nblocks = json.load(open('blocks2.json'))\nids = [699,703,705,720,726,727,730,734,735]\nfor i in ids:\n    k,t,p = blocks[i]\n    if k=='pagenum':\n        print(f\"===== {i} PAGEBREAK p={t} =====\")\n        continue\n    print(f\"===== {i} (p.{p}) len={len(t)} =====\")\n    print(\"END:\", t[-320:])\n    print()\nEOF"},"output":"===== 699 (p.36) len=1285 =====\nEND: lity to execute its strategic plan as an independent, stand-alone company (including Mac-Gray's ability to identify, acquire and successfully integrate laundry facilities management businesses, establish new and/or renew existing laundry facility management leases and penetrate markets historically dominated by smaller\n\n===== 703 (p.37) len=1666 =====\nEND: ve into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share and authorized the Transaction Committee and Goodwin Procter to negotiate the terms of such exclusivity based on guidance provided by the Special Committee. In addition, at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share.\n\n===== 705 (p.37) len=490 =====\nEND: clusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained, which we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee, agreements regarding certain post-signing covenants, the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was\n\n===== 720 (p.39) len=1155 =====\nEND: ns to their respective clients. Later that day, after various discussions among representatives from CSC/Pamplona, Kirkland, Goodwin Procter and the members of the Transaction Committee, and on behalf of the Special Committee, Goodwin Procter sent an e-mail to the representatives of Kirkland that proposed to accept the\n\n===== 726 (p.40) len=2250 =====\nEND:  Transaction Committee and representatives of Mac-Gray were authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, which represented approximately 3.2% of the total equity value of the transaction.\n\n===== 727 (p.40) len=279 =====\nEND: Later on October 11, 2013, the two members of the Transaction Committee telephoned CSC/Pamplona and communicated the Special Committee's position. Shortly following that conversation, the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray\n\n===== 730 (p.41) len=152 =====\nEND: termination fee. Following such agreement, Goodwin Procter delivered Kirkland revised drafts of the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter.\n\n===== 734 (p.41) len=2090 =====\nEND:  the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders and that the Board approve the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopt the merger agreement and recommend that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement. The Special Committee meeting then adjourned.\n\n===== 735 (p.41) len=874 =====\nEND: t the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders, approved the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopted the merger agreement and recommended that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement.\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"===== 699 (p.36) len=1285 =====\nEND: lity to execute its strategic plan as an independent, stand-alone company (including Mac-Gray's ability to identify, acquire and successfully integrate laundry facilities management businesses, establish new and/or renew existing laundry facility management leases and penetrate markets historically dominated by smaller\n\n===== 703 (p.37) len=1666 =====\nEND: ve into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share and authorized the Transaction Committee and Goodwin Procter to negotiate the terms of such exclusivity based on guidance provided by the Special Committee. In addition, at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share.\n\n===== 705 (p.37) len=490 =====\nEND: clusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained, which we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee, agreements regarding certain post-signing covenants, the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was\n\n===== 720 (p.39) len=1155 =====\nEND: ns to their respective clients. Later that day, after various discussions among representatives from CSC/Pamplona, Kirkland, Goodwin Procter and the members of the Transaction Committee, and on behalf of the Special Committee, Goodwin Procter sent an e-mail to the representatives of Kirkland that proposed to accept the\n\n===== 726 (p.40) len=2250 =====\nEND:  Transaction Committee and representatives of Mac-Gray were authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, which represented approximately 3.2% of the total equity value of the transaction.\n\n===== 727 (p.40) len=279 =====\nEND: Later on October 11, 2013, the two members of the Transaction Committee telephoned CSC/Pamplona and communicated the Special Committee's position. Shortly following that conversation, the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray\n\n===== 730 (p.41) len=152 =====\nEND: termination fee. Following such agreement, Goodwin Procter delivered Kirkland revised drafts of the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter.\n\n===== 734 (p.41) len=2090 =====\nEND:  the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders and that the Board approve the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopt the merger agreement and recommend that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement. The Special Committee meeting then adjourned.\n\n===== 735 (p.41) len=874 =====\nEND: t the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders, approved the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopted the merger agreement and recommended that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement.\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json\\nblocks = json.load(open('blocks2.json'))\\nids = [699,703,705,720,726,727,730,734,735]\\nfor i in ids:\\n    k,t,p = blocks[i]\\n    if k=='pagenum':\\n        print(f\\\"===== {i} PAGEBREAK p={t} =====\\\")\\n        continue\\n    print(f\\\"===== {i} (p.{p}) len={len(t)} =====\\\")\\n    print(\\\"END:\\\", t[-320:])\\n    print()\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824554822,"end":1789824555251}}}}
