Special Committee on 08/15/2013, sent once all four bidders' diligence was substantially complete) instructing revised written proposals no later than 09/09/2013 to continue in the process toward in-depth confirmatory diligence; requested valuation, sources and structures of financing, regulatory approvals and other post-signing covenants, and due-diligence focus areas.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(685, \"sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\", \"making a revised offer.\") +\n     \" Authorization: \" + Q(681, \"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona\", \"substantially complete requesting that\").strip() + \".\",\n src=CITE(681,685), main=685, review=\"Q2\", page=35, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,8,27), dto=D(2013,8,27), working=D(2013,8,27), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n due=D(2013,9,9), related=\"milestone R027\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/09/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\", what=\"Deadline\", round=2, type_=None,\n terms=\"Scheduled due date for revised written proposals. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on 09/09/2013; Party A and Party C on 09/10/2013 - all reviewed by the Special Committee on 09/11/2013 with no disclosed revision or extension: Late bids accepted.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(689, \"On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest\") + \"... \" +\n     Q(690, \"On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest\", \"an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share\") +\n     \" Review: \" + Q(692, \"the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona.\") +\n     \" Convention: Late bids accepted; continuation after the date without a disclosed extension is not a formal revision.\",\n src=CITE(689,690,692), main=689, review=\"Q2\", page=35, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,9), dto=D(2013,9,9), working=D(2013,9,9), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n due=D(2013,9,9), dtreat=\"Late bids accepted\",\n related=\"submissions R028, R029 (on time); R030, R031 (09/10)\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/09/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", round=2, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest: all cash $19.50 per share; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations with Mac-Gray.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(689, \"CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share, indicating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to exclusive negotiations for two weeks.\") +\n     \" Formality: revised IOI, no formal documentation or final-solicitation signal yet. Conditions: committed sponsor financing reported and no diligence condition stated (Light); diligence in fact still under way. Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\",\n src=CITE(689), main=689, review=\"Q5; Q6\", page=35, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,9), dto=D(2013,9,9), working=D(2013,9,9), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=19.50, phigh=19.50, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=19.50,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Light\",\n related=\"revises R018; revised by R035\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/09/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Bid\", round=2, type_=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest, all cash, $18.50 per share; proposed to finance with equity from affiliated funds plus third-party debt; no firm financing commitment.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(689, \"On September 9, 2013, Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share and proposed to finance the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt. Party B's revised indication of interest did not include a firm financing commitment.\") +\n     \" Formality: revised IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: reported absence of a firm commitment - Heavy. Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\",\n src=CITE(689,690), main=689, review=\"Q6\", page=35, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,9), dto=D(2013,9,9), working=D(2013,9,9), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=18.50,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n related=\"revises R020; revised by R037\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/10/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Bid\", round=2, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest, all cash, $18.00-$19.00 per share; to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(690, \"Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources.\") +\n     \" \" + Q(690, \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.\") +\n     \" Formality: revised IOI, no formal signal yet. Conditions: no firm commitment - Heavy. Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\",\n src=CITE(690), main=690, review=\"Q5; Q6\", page=35, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,10), dto=D(2013,9,10), working=D(2013,9,10), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=None,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n related=\"revises R008; reaffirmed R036; closed R043\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/10/2013\", who=\"Party C\", what=\"Bid\", round=2, type_=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Revised oral indication of interest, all cash, $16.00-$17.00 per share; no financing or condition information stated.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(690, \"a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share.\") +\n     \" Formality: revised IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: the filing reports the price but nothing about financing, diligence or other conditions, and the stage gives no further context - Insufficient evidence (preferred reading: no commitment reported; flagged Q6). Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\",\n src=CITE(690), main=690, review=\"Q6\", page=35, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,10), dto=D(2013,9,10), working=D(2013,9,10), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=16.00, phigh=17.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=None,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Insufficient evidence\",\n related=\"revises R023; non-submission R038\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/11/2013\", who=\"Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. (CEO)\", what=\"Material process update\", round=2, type_=None,\n terms=\"Rollover: Transaction Committee gave Mr. MacDonald a limited, unidentified overview (without names or prices) so he could consider rolling over shares; he decided he was not interested in any rollover; he was fully briefed in detail on 09/12/2013 and voiced general support for continuing the process but wanted Mac-Gray to seek a higher value. One row for the denied/resolved rollover step.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(691, \"During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction.\") +\n     \" Later: \" + Q(696, \"he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders.\") +\n     \" Context: \" + Q(692, \"it was unlikely that any of these parties would move forward in the process without the express support of Mr. MacDonald.\") +\n     \" Rollover rows carry no Count and no membership change.\",\n src=CITE(691,692,696), main=691, review=\"Q8\", page=35, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,11), dto=D(2013,9,11), working=D(2013,9,11), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n related=\"MacDonald voting agreement executed 09/27/2013 (part of R048)\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/11/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray Special Committee\", what=\"Round opened\", round=3, type_=None,\n terms=\"Round 3: first request for final indications of interest (due 09/18/2013) with a possible short period of exclusive negotiations depending on price and deal certainty; BofA Merrill Lynch called all four bidders the same day as authorized. Round finality: Announced as final - the target told the bidders this was the final-indication stage. Also that day: the Special Committee agreed Mr. MacDonald's support was critical, that he be fully briefed, and expected no bidder to proceed without his support.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(695, \"the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\", \"level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder's final proposal.\") +\n     \" \" + Q(695, \"As authorized and instructed by the Special Committee, representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch called each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona on September 11, 2013 with such instructions.\") +\n     \" Convention: the target's first request for final offers opens a new round even with unchanged bidders; Deadlines: due date set in the same instruction, carried on this row.\",\n src=CITE(692,695), main=695, review=\"Q1\", page=36, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,11), dto=D(2013,9,11), working=D(2013,9,11), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n due=D(2013,9,18), finality=\"Announced as final\",\n related=\"milestone R034; selection R039; rejected boundary candidate R041/R042\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\", what=\"Deadline\", round=3, type_=None,\n terms=\"Scheduled due date for final indications of interest. CSC/Pamplona, Party A and Party B responded on the date; Party C did not. The Special Committee took its next step on 09/19/2013, authorizing exclusive negotiation with CSC/Pamplona on the bids in hand: Enforced.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(698, \"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share\") +\n     \" and the Special Committee meeting of 09/19/2013: \" + Q(699, \"On September 19, 2013, the Special Committee held an in-person meeting.\") +\n     \" Convention: treatment Enforced - the date passed with no extension and no late acceptance, and the target took its next step (selection/exclusivity) on the bids in hand. Party C's non-response is recorded at R038.\",\n src=CITE(695,698,699), main=698, review=\"Q2\", page=36, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n due=D(2013,9,18), dtreat=\"Enforced\", related=\"submissions R035, R036, R037; non-submission R038\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", round=3, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"All-cash proposal at $20.75 per share; Pamplona's 100% capital commitment reiterated; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Formality: Formal (signal 2 - response on the requested basis to the final-indications solicitation); Conditions: Light (committed financing, no diligence condition stated); diligence still open.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(698, \"CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks.\") +\n     \" Convention: Formality signal 2 despite the non-binding IOI form; Conditions Light. Count 1 = first R3 submission by this unit.\",\n src=CITE(698), main=698, review=\"Q5; Q6\", page=36, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=20.75, phigh=20.75, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=20.75,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Light\",\n related=\"revises R028; revised to last-and-best R040\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Bid reaffirmed\", round=3, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Telephone confirmation that the $18.00-$19.00 indication stood as Party A's best and final offer; no improvement. Price carried forward from R030. Formality: Formal (signal 2 - response in the best-and-final stage; borderline, flagged Q5). Conditions reassessed: financing not committed; diligence open.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(698, \"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.\") +\n     \" Convention: recorded as Bid reaffirmed (actual bidder confirmation that its offer stands); price carried forward with origin Carried forward, not restated. Count 1 - first reaffirmation by this unit in round 3.\",\n src=CITE(698), main=698, review=\"Q5; Q6\", page=36, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Carried forward\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=None,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n related=\"reaffirms R030; closed R043\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Bid\", round=3, type_=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest that Party B valued at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash paid at closing plus options the bidder valued at $2.50 (options for 10% of new equity, strike at initial cost basis, vesting over five years on base-case management projections excluding future acquisitions). Cash component below CSC/Pamplona's $20.75; total above it but contingent/deferred; financing remained affiliated-fund equity plus third-party debt without a firm commitment. Price cells show the cash component and the bidder's stated total valuation (package, not a submitted range) - flagged Q7.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(698, \"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis.\") +\n     \" \" + Q(698, \"Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.\") +\n     \" Formality: signal 2 response to the final solicitation; Conditions: no firm financing commitment (Heavy); risk view in R039/R044. Count 1 = first R3 submission by this unit.\",\n src=CITE(698,702,703), main=698, review=\"Q5; Q6; Q7\", page=36, count=1,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=19.00, phigh=21.50, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"No\", cashclose=19.00,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n related=\"revises R029; closed R044\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"by 09/18/2013\", who=\"Party C\", what=\"Did not submit\", round=3, type_=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Stated non-submission at the final-indications solicitation: did not submit a revised indication or reiterate its prior $16.00-$17.00 indication, and gave no reasons; no notice, discouragement or withdrawal is reported. Decided by Unknown; exit reason Not stated (the filing states the fact, not the cause). Count 1 = this unit.\",\n count=1, decided=\"Unknown\", exitr=\"Not stated\", obasis=\"Stated\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(698, \"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith.\") +\n     \" Reported again: \" + Q(699, \"reported that Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest.\") +\n     \" Convention: non-submission is not a withdrawal and agency is not inferred from silence; recorded at the due date.\",\n src=CITE(698,699), main=698, review=\"Q4\", page=36,\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\"Relative only\", method=\"Assigned: deadline\",\n related=\"last bid R031; next recorded activity none\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- selection / round 4\nrow(\n when=\"09/19/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray Special Committee\", what=\"Target decision\", round=3, type_=None,\n terms=\"Preferred-bidder and exclusivity decision: the Special Committee concluded CSC/Pamplona's revised indication had the potential to deliver the most value with greater certainty and less risk than the alternatives (Party B's options contingent/deferred and Party B reliant on third-party debt; Party A's lower best-and-final); expected CSC/Pamplona to be able to increase above $20.75 given synergies; authorized the Transaction Committee to tell CSC/Pamplona Mac-Gray was prepared to move to exclusivity at $21.25 per share and to negotiate exclusivity terms; Mr. MacDonald said he would be supportive at $21.25. Not a round opening (a selection inside round 3).\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(703, \"the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications.\") +\n     \" \" + Q(703, \"authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share\") +\n     \" \" + Q(703, \"Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share.\") +\n     \" Convention: no Count on a process-wide decision.\",\n src=CITE(699,702,703), main=703, review=\"Q1\", page=37, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,19), dto=D(2013,9,19), working=D(2013,9,19), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n related=\"follows R034; leads to R040, R041\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/21/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", round=3, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Increase to $21.25 per share all cash as a last and best offer, provided Mac-Gray agree to a two-week exclusive negotiation; CSC/Pamplona also requested a voting agreement covering shares of Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family. Target proposed the price point on the same call; price revision solicited by the target after the due date belongs to the round's continuing negotiation. Count 0: same bidder and round as R035 - this is a revision, not a new unit.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(704, \"the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations. The representative of CSC/Pamplona also requested that shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned beneficially and of record by Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family be subject to a customary voting agreement\") +\n     \" Formality: carried forward from the formal R035 submission (price confirmation in final negotiation). Conditions: committed financing, no diligence condition stated (Light); diligence open.\",\n src=CITE(704,705), main=704, review=\"Q5; Q6\", page=37, count=0,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,21), dto=D(2013,9,21), working=D(2013,9,21), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n plow=21.25, phigh=21.25, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", curr=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=21.25,\n cond_detail=\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Light\",\n related=\"revises R035; basis of R041 and R048; voting-agreement request part of R048\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/24/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona (with Mac-Gray)\", what=\"Exclusivity changed\", round=4, type_=None,\n terms=\"Granted: exclusive negotiations until 5:00 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to CSC and Pamplona not adversely changing the final proposal terms, which included: no financing contingency; Pamplona committed to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing; a $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance is not obtained; certain post-signing covenants. Requested by CSC/Pamplona on 09/09 and 09/18; Special Committee authorized entering exclusivity on 09/23/2013 after CSC/Pamplona confirmed $21.25 as last and best on 09/21/2013. Dropped every other live bidder on the execution date (R043, R044).\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(711, \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.\") +\n     \" Terms: \" + Q(705, \"the inclusion of a $15 million\", \"we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee\") + \" and \" + Q(708, \"committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, which, together with the all-cash per share purchase price of $21.25, we refer to as the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.\") +\n     \" Exclusivity rows carry no Count.\",\n src=CITE(705,708,709,710,711), main=711, review=\"Q2; Q4\", page=38, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,24), dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n related=\"follows R040; opened R042; drops R043, R044; extended R047; basis of R048\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/24/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Round opened\", round=4, type_=None,\n terms=\"Round 4: exclusive negotiation and definitive-agreement stage with the selected bidder CSC/Pamplona, beginning with the executed exclusivity agreement; single-bidder stage (no organized competing solicitation). Round finality: Inferred final - the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder without a further finality announcement. Alternative boundary treatment (fold this stage into round 3) is listed in Q1.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(711, \"executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\") +\n     \" Next steps: \" + Q(712, \"Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona\", \"the initial draft of the merger agreement.\") +\n     \" Convention: a round can open when the target moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not be a new round.\",\n src=CITE(711,712), main=711, review=\"Q1\", page=38, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,24), dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n finality=\"Inferred final\", related=\"opens with R041; signed R048\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"by 09/24/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Dropped by target\", round=4, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Inferred: exclusivity - Party A was live when the target executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013 (last bid reaffirmed 09/18/2013 as best and final); the filing reports no notice to Party A. Decided by: Target; exit reason: Would not improve earlier offer (asked for final indications and declined to improve on $18.00-$19.00).\",\n count=1, decided=\"Target\", exitr=\"Would not improve earlier offer\", obasis=\"Inferred: exclusivity\",\n why=\"Stated execution: \" + Q(711, \"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\") +\n     \" Party A's last act: \" + Q(698, \"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.\") +\n     \" No notice to Party A is reported. Convention: executing exclusivity with one bidder closes every other bidder still live in the stage; the reason preserves the informative stated constraint without changing agency.\",\n src=CITE(711,698), main=711, review=\"Q4\", page=38,\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\"Relative only\", method=\"Assigned: decision day\",\n related=\"last bid R036; exclusivity R041\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"by 09/24/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Dropped by target\", round=4, type_=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Inferred: exclusivity - Party B was live when exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona was executed on 09/24/2013 (last proposal 09/18/2013, valued at $21.50 including options); the filing reports no notice to Party B. Decided by: Target; exit reason: Terms or process - the Special Committee cited the contingent/deferred options and the debt-financed structure as risks and preferred CSC/Pamplona's certainty.\",\n count=1, decided=\"Target\", exitr=\"Terms or process\", obasis=\"Inferred: exclusivity\",\n why=\"Stated execution: \" + Q(711, \"executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\") +\n     \" Stated reasoning: \" + Q(703, \"the indication of interest submitted by Party B, including the Party B options, was on its face higher than the CSC/Pamplona proposal\", \"which did not require any third party financing.\") +\n     \" No notice to Party B is reported. Convention: exclusivity execution closes live rivals.\",\n src=CITE(711,698,703), main=711, review=\"Q4\", page=38,\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\"Relative only\", method=\"Assigned: decision day\",\n related=\"last bid R037; exclusivity R041\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"09/25/2013-10/07/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Information access changed\", round=4, type_=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Once selected: CSC and Pamplona granted full access to the electronic data site and to certain members of management (previously limited as strategic bidders, with customer data withheld) and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence; confirmatory business-diligence meeting 10/01/2013. Access rows carry no Count.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(712, \"Also during this time, CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray.\") +\n     \" Timing: the passage sits between the 09/25/2013 initial merger-agreement draft and the 10/07/2013 Special Committee meeting; period start assigned as the Working date.\",\n src=CITE(712,716), main=712, review=\"Q1\", page=38, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,9,25), dto=D(2013,10,7), working=D(2013,9,25), basis=\"Reported interval\", method=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=\"earlier limited access R025; confirmatory diligence meeting R045 note\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"by 10/07/2013\", who=\"Moab (with CSC/Pamplona)\", what=\"Material process update\", round=4, type_=None,\n terms=\"Rollover resolved: after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona beginning 09/23/2013 (facilitated by BofA Merrill Lynch), it was determined that Moab would not roll over any Moab shares in the transaction; reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013. Moab later signed a voting agreement at signing (R048). Rollover rows carry no Count.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(718, \"Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.\") +\n     \" Origin: \" + Q(712, \"Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares.\") +\n     \" Date: the determination is reported only as made by this meeting; upper bound taken as the Working date.\",\n src=CITE(709,712,718), main=718, review=\"Q8\", page=39, count=None,\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,10,7), working=D(2013,10,7), basis=\"Relative only\", method=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=\"denial R014; voting agreement at signing R048\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"10/12/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona (with Mac-Gray)\", what=\"Exclusivity changed\", round=4, type_=None,\n terms=\"Extended: exclusivity was due to expire 5:00 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013; Kirkland requested an extension on CSC/Pamplona's behalf; the Special Committee authorized it on 10/09/2013 and again on 10/11/2013 (conditioned on a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, approximately 3.2% of total equity value) and the parties executed a letter agreement on 10/12/2013 extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013; the fee was agreed at $11 million on 10/11/2013. Exclusivity rows carry no Count.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(731, \"On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013.\") +\n     \" Authorization: \" + Q(725, \"Kirkland had requested on behalf of CSC/Pamplona that the exclusivity agreement, due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, be extended\", \"to extend exclusivity to October 15, 2013.\") +\n     \" Condition: \" + Q(726, \"authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, which represented approximately 3.2% of the total equity value of the transaction.\"),\n src=CITE(725,726,727,731), main=731, review=\"Q2\", page=41, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,10,12), dto=D(2013,10,12), working=D(2013,10,12), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n related=\"extends R041; fee history part of R048\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"10/14/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray; Spin Holdco Inc.; CSC Fenway, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.\", what=\"Merger agreement signed\", round=4, type_=None,\n terms=\"Signed definitive merger agreement: CSC Fenway, Inc. (Merger Subsidiary) merges into Mac-Gray, which survives as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Spin Holdco Inc. (Parent); each outstanding share converted into $21.25 in cash (all-cash; no financing condition). Pamplona commitment letter delivered ($594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P.; Pamplona jointly and severally liable with the Buyer Entities for breaches, its damages liability capped at $50 million, Buyer Entities unlimited). $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee / $15 million Parent termination fee. Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement; the MacDonald and family voting agreements became effective; stockholders entering voting agreements held approximately 15% of shares at the 11/27/2013 record date. End date 03/31/2014 (extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains); completion expected in the first half of 2014 (not observed in the filing). Signing is not an extra bid, so price/formality/condition cells are blank.\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(736, \"Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective.\") +\n     \" Terms: \" + Q(216, \"each outstanding share of Mac-Gray common stock\", \"converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes\") +\n     \" \" + Q(232, \"Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital\", \"Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013\") +\n     \" \" + Q(309, \"Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances\", \"Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances.\") +\n     \" \" + Q(322, \"the stockholders of Mac-Gray that entered into the voting agreements collectively owned approximately 15% of the Mac-Gray common stock entitled to vote at the special meeting.\") +\n     \" See X-001/X-002/X-005/X-016/X-028/X-029 for party and agreement definitions.\",\n src=CITE(734,736,173,215,216,232,282,309,312,322,1085,1101,1103), main=736, review=None, page=41, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,10,14), dto=D(2013,10,14), working=D(2013,10,14), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n related=\"concludes R040/R041/R042; announcement R049\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n\nrow(\n when=\"10/15/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.\", what=\"Merger announced\", round=4, type_=None,\n terms=\"Joint announcement by Mac-Gray and CSC before the U.S. stock markets opened. Post-signing status per the proxy: no competing proposal, go-shop or agreement termination disclosed; HSR waiting period expired 11/27/2013; merger litigation filed 11/21/2013 (see Summary; regulatory and litigation items are not separate ledger rows).\",\n why=\"Stated: \" + Q(737, \"On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement.\") +\n     \" Post-signing: \" + Q(324, \"While early termination was not granted, the waiting period expired on November 27, 2013.\") +\n     \" \" + Q(1540, \"On November 21, 2013, a putative class action lawsuit was filed\", \"captioned Star Partners Fund v. Bullock, et al. , Civ. 13-5067.\"),\n src=CITE(737,324,1538,1540), main=737, review=None, page=41, count=None,\n dfrom=D(2013,10,15), dto=D(2013,10,15), working=D(2013,10,15), basis=\"Reported day\", method=\"Reported\",\n related=\"follows R048\", deal=\"Mac-Gray\")\n","path":"/tmp/opencode/ledger_rows.py"},"output":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/ledger_rows.py","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/ledger_rows.py"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Ledger rows for the Mac-Gray / CSC deal (process 1, rounds 0-4).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom datetime import date\\nfrom ledger_data import Q, CITE\\n\\nD = date\\n\\nROWS = []\\ndef row(**kw):\\n    ROWS.append(kw)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- round 0 / context\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"10/23/2012\\\", who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Adviser engaged\\\", round=0, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Engaged by Mac-Gray as financial advisor for its consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC (the 2011-2012 Discussions - an attempted purchase by Mac-Gray, not its own sale). Mandate later terminated (Adviser ended row); the same bank is re-engaged for this sale process.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(623, \\\"Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Context only, per the instruction that a target's attempt to buy another company is not its own sale process; the engagement explains the adviser's later re-engagement for this sale process (R006).\\\",\\n src=CITE(623), main=623, review=\\\"Q8\\\", page=27, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2012,10,23), dto=D(2012,10,23), working=D(2012,10,23), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"terminated by R005; re-engaged in R006\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"04/05/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors\\\", what=\\\"Target sale decision\\\", round=0, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Board authorized management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities, including opportunities with Party A; discussed the sale of CSC to Pamplona and industry M&A activity; to revisit strategic alternatives on 05/09/2013. An exploration authorization, not the sale-process launch (see R009).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(624, \\\"authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities\\\", \\\"in the laundry facilities management industry\\\") +\\n     \\\" Qualification: the Board only \\\" + Q(624, \\\"determined to further consider Mac-Gray's strategic alternatives at its meeting scheduled for May 9, 2013.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Counting: no tally contribution (process-wide decision row).\\\",\\n src=CITE(624), main=624, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=27, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,4,5), dto=D(2013,4,5), working=D(2013,4,5), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"followed by R003 contact and R009 sale-process opening\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"04/08/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Contact\\\", round=0, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Direction: target-initiated (BofA Merrill Lynch telephoned, as instructed by the Board). First sale-related contact; Party A indicated it might consider a business combination with Mac-Gray. Pre-process (round 0).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(625, \\\"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A\\\", \\\"possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Count 1 = the newly represented bidder unit for the contact step; the same bidder's 06/21/2013 Bid row (R008) adds no second contact count.\\\",\\n src=CITE(625), main=625, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=27, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,4,8), dto=D(2013,4,8), working=D(2013,4,8), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"same bidder later bids (R008) and signs NDA (R024)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"05/09/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors\\\", what=\\\"Material process update\\\", round=0, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Board reviewed the sale-process option (risks/benefits, potential disruption, leak risk, disclosure to competitors) alongside standalone alternatives; formed a Transaction Committee (Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust) to administer the strategic-alternatives review and recommend a financial adviser; deferred a decision to the next meeting.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(626, \\\"the Board formed a transaction committee at this meeting\\\", \\\"to serve as its members.\\\") +\\n     \\\" No sale decision or outreach yet; recorded because the governance step structures the process that follows.\\\",\\n src=CITE(626), main=626, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=27, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,5,9), dto=D(2013,5,9), working=D(2013,5,9), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"leads to adviser selection (R006) and sale decision (R009)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"05/15/2013\\\", who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Adviser ended\\\", round=0, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Termination of the 2011-2012 Discussions engagement: the Transaction Committee determined on 05/14/2013 to terminate; Mac-Gray sent the termination letter 05/15/2013. Not a termination of the sale process (which had not begun).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(636, \\\"On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Determination: \\\" + Q(635, \\\"the Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch's engagement letter\\\", \\\"2011-2012 Discussions.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Adviser rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n src=CITE(635,636), main=636, review=\\\"Q8\\\", page=29, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,5,15), dto=D(2013,5,15), working=D(2013,5,15), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"ends the R001 mandate; new mandate in R006\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"05/30/2013\\\", who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Adviser engaged\\\", round=0, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Mac-Gray's financial advisor for the strategic-alternatives review and sale process; Board unanimously approved the engagement on 05/30/2013; engagement letter entered 05/31/2013; BofA agreed not to engage as a possible source of new acquisition financing for any potential buyer without Mac-Gray's prior written consent. Three nationally recognized banks were invited to submit proposals; the other two presented 05/29/2013.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(640, \\\"the Board unanimously approved the engagement of BofA Merrill Lynch on the terms discussed at this meeting.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Engagement letter: \\\" + Q(645, \\\"On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", \\\"without Mac-Gray's prior written consent.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Adviser rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n src=CITE(640,645), main=640, review=\\\"Q8\\\", page=29, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,5,30), dto=D(2013,5,30), working=D(2013,5,30), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"replaces the terminated R001 mandate\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"05/30/2013\\\", who=\\\"Moab Partners, L.P. and affiliates\\\", what=\\\"Activist involvement\\\", round=0, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Proxy contest led to the election of Moab's nominees Michael M. Rothenberg and James E. Hyman at the annual meeting later on 05/30/2013 (in place of two incumbent nominees); Board reduced to seven; Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding stock as of 06/12/2013. Mr. Rothenberg was later excluded from sale-process deliberations and engaged over a possible equity rollover (R014, R046).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(641, \\\"Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees\\\") +\\n     \\\" Ownership: \\\" + Q(646, \\\"At the time of this meeting, Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding common stock.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Activist rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n src=CITE(641,646), main=641, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=29, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,5,30), dto=D(2013,5,30), working=D(2013,5,30), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"context for R014 and R046 rollover rows\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- round 0 bid / round 1\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"06/21/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=0, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Unsolicited all-cash proposal to purchase Mac-Gray at $17.00-$19.00 per share, submitted to the Board before any confidentiality agreement. Pre-process (round 0); retained as a genuine pre-NDA offer and shown as a standing round-1 proposal (see R009). No formal documentation signal; financing not stated.\\\",\\n why=Q(647, \\\"On June 21, 2013, Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors\\\", \\\"an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: preliminary pre-NDA indication without a supported formal signal. Conditions: preliminary non-binding indication before any substantive diligence access (no data-room or management access before 08/2013), so Heavy by context; financing not addressed. Price Stated; range endpoints retained, not averaged.\\\",\\n src=CITE(647), main=647, review=\\\"Q1; Q5; Q6\\\", page=30, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,6,21), dto=D(2013,6,21), working=D(2013,6,21), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=17.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"first contact R003; revised by R030; standing proposal counted in R1 (R009)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"06/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors; Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Round opened\\\", round=1, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"R1 anchor: 06/24/2013 Special Committee decision to consider a sale and authorize solicitation of 50 parties - outreach followed within about a week (first reported NDA 06/28/2013); other candidate anchors rejected: R008 (06/21/2013 Party A proposal), R012 (06/28/2013 first NDA); first outreach-wave date itself not disclosed. Sale consideration concluded in stockholders' best interests; Special Committee of six independent directors established (Bullock, Daoust, Hyman, Meagher, Percelay, Robinson; Mr. Bullock chairman); Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg excluded from sale-process evaluation and negotiations; the Transaction Committee became the Special Committee's sub-committee. Round finality: Not final (preliminary IOI solicitation; no finality signal).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(652, \\\"The Special Committee concluded that it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray\\\") +\\n     \\\" Scope: \\\" + Q(653, \\\"the Special Committee determined to approach a total of\\\", \\\"including private equity firms.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: anchor chosen under instruction rule 2 (the first outreach wave is undated; the filing reports the outreach as direct execution of the 06/24/2013 decision beginning within days). Special Committee formation and exclusions: \\\" + Q(648, \\\"the Board then established the Special Committee\\\", \\\"Mr. Bullock was appointed chairman of the Special Committee.\\\"),\\n src=CITE(648,651,652,653,656), main=648, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=30, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,6,24), dto=D(2013,6,24), working=D(2013,6,24), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n finality=\\\"Not final\\\", related=\\\"candidate anchors R008, R012; deadline set R010\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"by 07/23/2013; communication day not disclosed (packages furnished from 06/28/2013)\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Deadline set\\\", round=1, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Preliminary indications of interest due 07/23/2013; parties signing confidentiality and standstill agreements were furnished an informational package and instructed to submit by that date. The letter asked proposals to address valuation, sources and structures of financing, material conditions (including required approvals) and due-diligence focus areas.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(657, \\\"Parties that had entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with Mac-Gray were furnished an informational package\\\", \\\"which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Date: the communication day is not disclosed; Working date assigned by sequence (this row follows the 06/24/2013 round opening, R009). Due date is the only bid-submission clock recorded here.\\\",\\n src=CITE(657), main=657, review=\\\"Q2; Q8\\\", page=32, count=None,\\n dfrom=None, dto=None, working=D(2013,6,24), basis=\\\"Undated\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: sequence\\\",\\n due=D(2013,7,23), related=\\\"milestone R017\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"06/28/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Contact\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Direction: target-initiated (BofA Merrill Lynch spoke with Pamplona as instructed by the Special Committee). Pamplona expressed interest in a transaction, including an acquisition by portfolio company CSC; said business and legal due diligence would be minimal given familiarity with Mac-Gray and the industry. First reported contact with the winning bidder unit.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(658, \\\"BofA Merrill Lynch also reported that they had spoken with representatives of Pamplona\\\", \\\"including an acquisition of Mac-Gray by its portfolio company, CSC.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(658, \\\"Pamplona emphasized that business and legal due diligence would be minimal\\\", \\\"industry generally.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Count 1 = the newly represented bidder unit for the contact step.\\\",\\n src=CITE(658), main=658, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=32, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,6,28), dto=D(2013,6,28), working=D(2013,6,28), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"NDA R015; bidding through R040; winner\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"06/28/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray (Mac-Gray form; terms individually negotiated but not materially varied); furnished the informational package to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. New signer; NDA count 1.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(659, \\\"Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\\\", \\\"preliminary indication of interest.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Form and standstill terms: \\\" + Q(657, \\\"entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray\\\", \\\"did not vary materially from the form provided.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Count 1 = newly represented signer.\\\",\\n src=CITE(659,657), main=659, review=\\\"Q3\\\", page=32, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,6,28), dto=D(2013,6,28), working=D(2013,6,28), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"bid R020, R029, R037\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"06/30/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; furnished the informational package to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. New signer; NDA count 1.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(660, \\\"On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\\\", \\\"preliminary indication of interest.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Count 1 = newly represented signer.\\\",\\n src=CITE(660,657), main=660, review=\\\"Q3\\\", page=32, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,6,30), dto=D(2013,6,30), working=D(2013,6,30), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"bids R021, R023, R031; exit R038\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/06/2013\\\", who=\\\"Moab (with Mac-Gray Special Committee)\\\", what=\\\"Material process update\\\", round=1, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Rollover: Special Committee denied, at this stage, Moab's request to partner exclusively with CSC/Pamplona and to discuss an equity rollover; instructed BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter to communicate that rollover discussions were premature but would be permitted at a later stage, so Moab's shares could remain available as a capital source for other bidders. Denial step of this rollover relationship (resolution in R046).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(662, \\\"The Special Committee discussed whether Moab should be permitted to partner exclusively with CSC/Pamplona.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Decision: \\\" + Q(665, \\\"the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process so that\\\", \\\"other potential bidders.\\\") +\\n     \\\" One row permitted for the denied step of a rollover relationship; no Count.\\\",\\n src=CITE(661,662,665), main=662, review=\\\"Q8\\\", page=32, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,6), dto=D(2013,7,6), working=D(2013,7,6), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"resolved by R046; Moab voting agreement at signing (R048)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/11/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; furnished the informational package to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. New signer; NDA count 1.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(666, \\\"On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package\\\", \\\"preliminary indication of interest.\\\") +\\n     \\\" First bid follows 07/23/2013 (R018). Count 1 = newly represented signer.\\\",\\n src=CITE(666,657), main=666, review=\\\"Q3\\\", page=33, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,11), dto=D(2013,7,11), working=D(2013,7,11), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"winning bidder unit; signing R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"between 06/28/2013 and 08/05/2013 (individuated signings; the filing reports the 20 signings only in aggregate over the two months following the 06/24/2013 directive)\\\",\\n who=\\\"16 remaining NDA signers (financial; residual cohort)\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Disjoint residual cohort: 20 NDA signers reported in total minus the four individually recorded signers (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) = 16 remaining financial signers. No individual dates, names or terms; signing window bounded by the first and last individually recorded signings (06/28/2013 to 08/05/2013).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated base and split: \\\" + Q(657, \\\"a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\\\") +\\n     \\\" Arithmetic: 20 - 4 individually recorded = 16 financial signers. Date: individual dates not disclosed; window bounded by R012 (06/28/2013) and R024 (08/05/2013); Working date by midpoint convention. Count 16 is the residual tally contribution for the NDA step, not a new population.\\\",\\n src=CITE(657,659,660,666,676), main=657, review=\\\"Q3; Q8\\\", page=32, count=16,\\n dfrom=D(2013,6,28), dto=D(2013,8,5), working=D(2013,7,17), basis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: midpoint\\\",\\n related=\\\"covered individually by R012, R013, R015, R024; closed in R019\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/23/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Deadline\\\", round=1, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Scheduled due date for preliminary indications of interest. CSC/Pamplona submitted on 07/23/2013; Party B submitted 07/24/2013 and Party C orally 07/24/2013 (written 07/25/2013). The Special Committee reviewed Party B's, Party C's and CSC/Pamplona's submissions plus Party A's standing 06/21/2013 proposal on 07/25/2013 with no disclosed revision or extension: Late bids accepted.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(657, \\\"instructed to submit by July 23, 2013.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Late bids: \\\" + Q(669, \\\"On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Considered: \\\" + Q(670, \\\"reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: treatment is Late bids accepted - the target considered post-due-date bids without any revision; continuation without a disclosed extension is not a revised due date.\\\",\\n src=CITE(657,668,669,670), main=657, review=\\\"Q2\\\", page=32, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,23), dto=D(2013,7,23), working=D(2013,7,23), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n due=D(2013,7,23), dtreat=\\\"Late bids accepted\\\",\\n related=\\\"on-time bid R018; later bids R020, R021\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/23/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"All-cash preliminary indication of interest at $18.50 per share; submitted after NDA (07/11/2013), before substantive diligence access; no financing commitment stated at this date.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(668, \\\"On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: preliminary IOI without a formal documentation or solicitation signal. Conditions: preliminary non-binding indication before data-room or management access, Heavy by context; financing not stated. Count 1 = first R1 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(668), main=668, review=\\\"Q6\\\", page=33, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,23), dto=D(2013,7,23), working=D(2013,7,23), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=18.50,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revised by R028; on-time for R017\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"by 07/23/2013\\\", who=\\\"16 remaining NDA signers (financial; residual cohort)\\\", what=\\\"Did not submit\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Inferred: residual (base assumes all 20 NDA signers were eligible for the 07/23/2013 preliminary solicitation; signers whose NDAs post-date that date would reduce the residual - flagged Q3) - 20 signers - 3 submitters (Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) - 1 continuing standing proposal (Party A) = 16 non-submitters. No identities, notices or motives inferred.\\\",\\n count=16, decided=\\\"Unknown\\\", exitr=\\\"Not stated\\\", obasis=\\\"Inferred: residual\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated base: \\\" + Q(657, \\\"a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\\\") +\\n     \\\" Accounting at the first transition: \\\" + Q(670, \\\"reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: residual close-out row (Count = stated base - participants accounted for). Agency is not inferred from an arithmetic non-submission; a participant closed here is not closed again unless it re-entered.\\\",\\n src=CITE(670,657,668,669), main=670, review=\\\"Q3; Q4\\\", page=33, count=None,\\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,7,23), working=D(2013,7,23), basis=\\\"Relative only\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: deadline\\\",\\n related=\\\"exit for the R016 cohort; same 16 persons as R016 (different step)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Preliminary indication of interest, all cash, $17.00-$18.00 per share; submitted one day after the due date (accepted; see R017); before data-room or management access.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(669, \\\"On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: preliminary IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: before substantive diligence access, Heavy by context; financing not stated. Count 1 = first R1 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(669), main=669, review=\\\"Q6\\\", page=33, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,24), dto=D(2013,7,24), working=D(2013,7,24), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=17.00, phigh=18.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revised by R029; later package R037\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=1, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Oral preliminary indication of interest, all cash, $15.00-$17.00 per share; submitted one day after the due date (accepted; see R017); before data-room or management access. Superseded by its written IOI the next day (R023).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(669, \\\"representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: preliminary oral IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: before substantive diligence access, Heavy by context; financing not stated. Count 1 = first R1 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(669), main=669, review=\\\"Q6\\\", page=33, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,24), dto=D(2013,7,24), working=D(2013,7,24), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=15.00, phigh=17.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revised by R023; later bid R031\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- round 2\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/25/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Round opened\\\", round=2, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Round 2: staged information access and management meetings for the four interested bidders (Party A conditional on signing a confidentiality agreement), then revised indications of interest. Preliminary IOIs judged lower than expected; Special Committee directed staged disclosure keyed to demonstrated seriousness; customer data withheld because of concern over strategic-bidder misuse; Mr. Rothenberg asked to recuse himself from Board meetings for the duration of the process. Round finality: Not final (revised-IOI stage; no finality signal). Alternative anchor candidates (rejected): R026 (08/27/2013 letter; due 09/09/2013) and the 08/15/2013 authorization.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(671, \\\"the Special Committee concluded that it would be advisable to stage the disclosure of such information to each of the bidders\\\", \\\"terms viewed favorably by the Special Committee.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Authorization: \\\" + Q(674, \\\"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: round opens where the target selects advancing participants and opens a distinct information stage linked to new offers.\\\",\\n src=CITE(670,671,674), main=674, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=34, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,25), dto=D(2013,7,25), working=D(2013,7,25), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n finality=\\\"Not final\\\", related=\\\"rejected anchor candidates R026 and 08/15 authorization; access R025; deadline set R026\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"07/25/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Written indication of interest, all cash, $16.00-$16.50 per share (replaces the $15.00-$17.00 oral range); submitted later on 07/25/2013. Count 0: same bidder and round as R021 - the written IOI is the same bid, not a second unit.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(675, \\\"Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: preliminary IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: before substantive diligence access (management presentation 08/08/2013), Heavy by context; financing not stated.\\\",\\n src=CITE(675), main=675, review=\\\"Q6\\\", page=34, count=0,\\n dfrom=D(2013,7,25), dto=D(2013,7,25), working=D(2013,7,25), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=16.00, phigh=16.50, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R021; later bid R031\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"08/05/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Confidentiality and standstill agreement after extended negotiation of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions (negotiations from 07/11/2013; impasse reported 07/23/2013; resumed 07/27/2013); furnished the informational package to potentially improve the Party A June 21 proposal. New signer; NDA count 1.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(676, \\\"Discussions with Party A resumed on July 27, 2103 and Party A and the Transaction Committee agreed to the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions. On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray\\\") +\\n     \\\" Impasse detail: \\\" + Q(667, \\\"outside counsel to Party A and representatives of Goodwin Procter negotiated the terms of a confidentiality and standstill agreement, but did not come to agreement on the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Source typo '2103' retained; proposed corrected date 2013 (context 07/11/2013 - 08/05/2013, flagged Q8). Count 1 = newly represented signer.\\\",\\n src=CITE(676,667), main=676, review=\\\"Q3; Q8\\\", page=34, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,8,5), dto=D(2013,8,5), working=D(2013,8,5), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"same bidder as R008; bids R030, R036\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"08/06/2013-08/27/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A; Party B; Party C; CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Information access changed\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Unknown\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Differential access during diligence: Party B and Party C (financial bidders) given broad access to the electronic data site; Party A and CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidders) given somewhat limited access; customer data (including customer locations) reserved until later in the process; both strategic bidders held synergy discussions with management. Management presentations were given to all four (Party B 08/06, Party C 08/08, CSC/Pamplona 08/12, Party A 08/14). Stated reason: prevent access to and misuse of sensitive competitive information by strategic bidders, staging disclosure by demonstrated seriousness. Participants are of mixed types (two strategic, two financial), so Type is recorded Unknown. Access rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(682, \\\"Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site\\\", \\\"as part of the staging discussed at the July 25 th Special Committee meeting.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Reason: \\\" + Q(671, \\\"expressed concern over permitting access to and the potential misuse of sensitive and competitive information, including customer terms and locations, especially by strategic bidders.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: one row per access decision; uniform management presentations belong to the stage that admitted all four (R022), not to a per-meeting row.\\\",\\n src=CITE(677,678,679,680,682,671), main=682, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=34, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,8,6), dto=D(2013,8,27), working=D(2013,8,6), basis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=\\\"stage opened R022; full access later R045\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"08/27/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Deadline set\\\", round=2, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Letter to Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona (authorized by the Special Committee on 08/15/2013, sent once all four bidders' diligence was substantially complete) instructing revised written proposals no later than 09/09/2013 to continue in the process toward in-depth confirmatory diligence; requested valuation, sources and structures of financing, regulatory approvals and other post-signing covenants, and due-diligence focus areas.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(685, \\\"sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\\\", \\\"making a revised offer.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Authorization: \\\" + Q(681, \\\"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona\\\", \\\"substantially complete requesting that\\\").strip() + \\\".\\\",\\n src=CITE(681,685), main=685, review=\\\"Q2\\\", page=35, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,8,27), dto=D(2013,8,27), working=D(2013,8,27), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n due=D(2013,9,9), related=\\\"milestone R027\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/09/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Deadline\\\", round=2, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Scheduled due date for revised written proposals. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on 09/09/2013; Party A and Party C on 09/10/2013 - all reviewed by the Special Committee on 09/11/2013 with no disclosed revision or extension: Late bids accepted.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(689, \\\"On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest\\\") + \\\"... \\\" +\\n     Q(690, \\\"On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest\\\", \\\"an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share\\\") +\\n     \\\" Review: \\\" + Q(692, \\\"the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: Late bids accepted; continuation after the date without a disclosed extension is not a formal revision.\\\",\\n src=CITE(689,690,692), main=689, review=\\\"Q2\\\", page=35, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,9), dto=D(2013,9,9), working=D(2013,9,9), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n due=D(2013,9,9), dtreat=\\\"Late bids accepted\\\",\\n related=\\\"submissions R028, R029 (on time); R030, R031 (09/10)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/09/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest: all cash $19.50 per share; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations with Mac-Gray.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(689, \\\"CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share, indicating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to exclusive negotiations for two weeks.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: revised IOI, no formal documentation or final-solicitation signal yet. Conditions: committed sponsor financing reported and no diligence condition stated (Light); diligence in fact still under way. Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(689), main=689, review=\\\"Q5; Q6\\\", page=35, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,9), dto=D(2013,9,9), working=D(2013,9,9), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=19.50, phigh=19.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=19.50,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Light\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R018; revised by R035\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/09/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest, all cash, $18.50 per share; proposed to finance with equity from affiliated funds plus third-party debt; no firm financing commitment.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(689, \\\"On September 9, 2013, Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share and proposed to finance the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt. Party B's revised indication of interest did not include a firm financing commitment.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: revised IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: reported absence of a firm commitment - Heavy. Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(689,690), main=689, review=\\\"Q6\\\", page=35, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,9), dto=D(2013,9,9), working=D(2013,9,9), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=18.50,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R020; revised by R037\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/10/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest, all cash, $18.00-$19.00 per share; to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(690, \\\"Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(690, \\\"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: revised IOI, no formal signal yet. Conditions: no firm commitment - Heavy. Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(690), main=690, review=\\\"Q5; Q6\\\", page=35, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,10), dto=D(2013,9,10), working=D(2013,9,10), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R008; reaffirmed R036; closed R043\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/10/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=2, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised oral indication of interest, all cash, $16.00-$17.00 per share; no financing or condition information stated.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(690, \\\"a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: revised IOI, no formal signal. Conditions: the filing reports the price but nothing about financing, diligence or other conditions, and the stage gives no further context - Insufficient evidence (preferred reading: no commitment reported; flagged Q6). Count 1 = first R2 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(690), main=690, review=\\\"Q6\\\", page=35, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,10), dto=D(2013,9,10), working=D(2013,9,10), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=16.00, phigh=17.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Insufficient evidence\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R023; non-submission R038\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/11/2013\\\", who=\\\"Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. (CEO)\\\", what=\\\"Material process update\\\", round=2, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Rollover: Transaction Committee gave Mr. MacDonald a limited, unidentified overview (without names or prices) so he could consider rolling over shares; he decided he was not interested in any rollover; he was fully briefed in detail on 09/12/2013 and voiced general support for continuing the process but wanted Mac-Gray to seek a higher value. One row for the denied/resolved rollover step.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(691, \\\"During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Later: \\\" + Q(696, \\\"he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Context: \\\" + Q(692, \\\"it was unlikely that any of these parties would move forward in the process without the express support of Mr. MacDonald.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Rollover rows carry no Count and no membership change.\\\",\\n src=CITE(691,692,696), main=691, review=\\\"Q8\\\", page=35, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,11), dto=D(2013,9,11), working=D(2013,9,11), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"MacDonald voting agreement executed 09/27/2013 (part of R048)\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/11/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Round opened\\\", round=3, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Round 3: first request for final indications of interest (due 09/18/2013) with a possible short period of exclusive negotiations depending on price and deal certainty; BofA Merrill Lynch called all four bidders the same day as authorized. Round finality: Announced as final - the target told the bidders this was the final-indication stage. Also that day: the Special Committee agreed Mr. MacDonald's support was critical, that he be fully briefed, and expected no bidder to proceed without his support.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(695, \\\"the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\\\", \\\"level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder's final proposal.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(695, \\\"As authorized and instructed by the Special Committee, representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch called each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona on September 11, 2013 with such instructions.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: the target's first request for final offers opens a new round even with unchanged bidders; Deadlines: due date set in the same instruction, carried on this row.\\\",\\n src=CITE(692,695), main=695, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=36, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,11), dto=D(2013,9,11), working=D(2013,9,11), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n due=D(2013,9,18), finality=\\\"Announced as final\\\",\\n related=\\\"milestone R034; selection R039; rejected boundary candidate R041/R042\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Deadline\\\", round=3, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Scheduled due date for final indications of interest. CSC/Pamplona, Party A and Party B responded on the date; Party C did not. The Special Committee took its next step on 09/19/2013, authorizing exclusive negotiation with CSC/Pamplona on the bids in hand: Enforced.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(698, \\\"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share\\\") +\\n     \\\" and the Special Committee meeting of 09/19/2013: \\\" + Q(699, \\\"On September 19, 2013, the Special Committee held an in-person meeting.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: treatment Enforced - the date passed with no extension and no late acceptance, and the target took its next step (selection/exclusivity) on the bids in hand. Party C's non-response is recorded at R038.\\\",\\n src=CITE(695,698,699), main=698, review=\\\"Q2\\\", page=36, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n due=D(2013,9,18), dtreat=\\\"Enforced\\\", related=\\\"submissions R035, R036, R037; non-submission R038\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=3, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"All-cash proposal at $20.75 per share; Pamplona's 100% capital commitment reiterated; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Formality: Formal (signal 2 - response on the requested basis to the final-indications solicitation); Conditions: Light (committed financing, no diligence condition stated); diligence still open.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(698, \\\"CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: Formality signal 2 despite the non-binding IOI form; Conditions Light. Count 1 = first R3 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(698), main=698, review=\\\"Q5; Q6\\\", page=36, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=20.75, phigh=20.75, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=20.75,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Light\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R028; revised to last-and-best R040\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Bid reaffirmed\\\", round=3, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Telephone confirmation that the $18.00-$19.00 indication stood as Party A's best and final offer; no improvement. Price carried forward from R030. Formality: Formal (signal 2 - response in the best-and-final stage; borderline, flagged Q5). Conditions reassessed: financing not committed; diligence open.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(698, \\\"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: recorded as Bid reaffirmed (actual bidder confirmation that its offer stands); price carried forward with origin Carried forward, not restated. Count 1 - first reaffirmation by this unit in round 3.\\\",\\n src=CITE(698), main=698, review=\\\"Q5; Q6\\\", page=36, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Carried forward\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=None,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"reaffirms R030; closed R043\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=3, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest that Party B valued at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash paid at closing plus options the bidder valued at $2.50 (options for 10% of new equity, strike at initial cost basis, vesting over five years on base-case management projections excluding future acquisitions). Cash component below CSC/Pamplona's $20.75; total above it but contingent/deferred; financing remained affiliated-fund equity plus third-party debt without a firm commitment. Price cells show the cash component and the bidder's stated total valuation (package, not a submitted range) - flagged Q7.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(698, \\\"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(698, \\\"Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: signal 2 response to the final solicitation; Conditions: no firm financing commitment (Heavy); risk view in R039/R044. Count 1 = first R3 submission by this unit.\\\",\\n src=CITE(698,702,703), main=698, review=\\\"Q5; Q6; Q7\\\", page=36, count=1,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,18), dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=19.00, phigh=21.50, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"No\\\", cashclose=19.00,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: none\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R029; closed R044\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"by 09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Did not submit\\\", round=3, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Stated non-submission at the final-indications solicitation: did not submit a revised indication or reiterate its prior $16.00-$17.00 indication, and gave no reasons; no notice, discouragement or withdrawal is reported. Decided by Unknown; exit reason Not stated (the filing states the fact, not the cause). Count 1 = this unit.\\\",\\n count=1, decided=\\\"Unknown\\\", exitr=\\\"Not stated\\\", obasis=\\\"Stated\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(698, \\\"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Reported again: \\\" + Q(699, \\\"reported that Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: non-submission is not a withdrawal and agency is not inferred from silence; recorded at the due date.\\\",\\n src=CITE(698,699), main=698, review=\\\"Q4\\\", page=36,\\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,9,18), working=D(2013,9,18), basis=\\\"Relative only\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: deadline\\\",\\n related=\\\"last bid R031; next recorded activity none\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- selection / round 4\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/19/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Target decision\\\", round=3, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Preferred-bidder and exclusivity decision: the Special Committee concluded CSC/Pamplona's revised indication had the potential to deliver the most value with greater certainty and less risk than the alternatives (Party B's options contingent/deferred and Party B reliant on third-party debt; Party A's lower best-and-final); expected CSC/Pamplona to be able to increase above $20.75 given synergies; authorized the Transaction Committee to tell CSC/Pamplona Mac-Gray was prepared to move to exclusivity at $21.25 per share and to negotiate exclusivity terms; Mr. MacDonald said he would be supportive at $21.25. Not a round opening (a selection inside round 3).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(703, \\\"the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(703, \\\"authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(703, \\\"Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: no Count on a process-wide decision.\\\",\\n src=CITE(699,702,703), main=703, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=37, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,19), dto=D(2013,9,19), working=D(2013,9,19), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"follows R034; leads to R040, R041\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/21/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", round=3, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Increase to $21.25 per share all cash as a last and best offer, provided Mac-Gray agree to a two-week exclusive negotiation; CSC/Pamplona also requested a voting agreement covering shares of Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family. Target proposed the price point on the same call; price revision solicited by the target after the due date belongs to the round's continuing negotiation. Count 0: same bidder and round as R035 - this is a revision, not a new unit.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(704, \\\"the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations. The representative of CSC/Pamplona also requested that shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned beneficially and of record by Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family be subject to a customary voting agreement\\\") +\\n     \\\" Formality: carried forward from the formal R035 submission (price confirmation in final negotiation). Conditions: committed financing, no diligence condition stated (Light); diligence open.\\\",\\n src=CITE(704,705), main=704, review=\\\"Q5; Q6\\\", page=37, count=0,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,21), dto=D(2013,9,21), working=D(2013,9,21), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n plow=21.25, phigh=21.25, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", curr=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=21.25,\\n cond_detail=\\\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Light\\\",\\n related=\\\"revises R035; basis of R041 and R048; voting-agreement request part of R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona (with Mac-Gray)\\\", what=\\\"Exclusivity changed\\\", round=4, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Granted: exclusive negotiations until 5:00 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to CSC and Pamplona not adversely changing the final proposal terms, which included: no financing contingency; Pamplona committed to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing; a $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance is not obtained; certain post-signing covenants. Requested by CSC/Pamplona on 09/09 and 09/18; Special Committee authorized entering exclusivity on 09/23/2013 after CSC/Pamplona confirmed $21.25 as last and best on 09/21/2013. Dropped every other live bidder on the execution date (R043, R044).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(711, \\\"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Terms: \\\" + Q(705, \\\"the inclusion of a $15 million\\\", \\\"we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee\\\") + \\\" and \\\" + Q(708, \\\"committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, which, together with the all-cash per share purchase price of $21.25, we refer to as the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Exclusivity rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n src=CITE(705,708,709,710,711), main=711, review=\\\"Q2; Q4\\\", page=38, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,24), dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"follows R040; opened R042; drops R043, R044; extended R047; basis of R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Round opened\\\", round=4, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Round 4: exclusive negotiation and definitive-agreement stage with the selected bidder CSC/Pamplona, beginning with the executed exclusivity agreement; single-bidder stage (no organized competing solicitation). Round finality: Inferred final - the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder without a further finality announcement. Alternative boundary treatment (fold this stage into round 3) is listed in Q1.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(711, \\\"executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\\\") +\\n     \\\" Next steps: \\\" + Q(712, \\\"Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona\\\", \\\"the initial draft of the merger agreement.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Convention: a round can open when the target moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not be a new round.\\\",\\n src=CITE(711,712), main=711, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=38, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,24), dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n finality=\\\"Inferred final\\\", related=\\\"opens with R041; signed R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"by 09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Dropped by target\\\", round=4, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity - Party A was live when the target executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013 (last bid reaffirmed 09/18/2013 as best and final); the filing reports no notice to Party A. Decided by: Target; exit reason: Would not improve earlier offer (asked for final indications and declined to improve on $18.00-$19.00).\\\",\\n count=1, decided=\\\"Target\\\", exitr=\\\"Would not improve earlier offer\\\", obasis=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated execution: \\\" + Q(711, \\\"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\\\") +\\n     \\\" Party A's last act: \\\" + Q(698, \\\"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.\\\") +\\n     \\\" No notice to Party A is reported. Convention: executing exclusivity with one bidder closes every other bidder still live in the stage; the reason preserves the informative stated constraint without changing agency.\\\",\\n src=CITE(711,698), main=711, review=\\\"Q4\\\", page=38,\\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\\\"Relative only\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: decision day\\\",\\n related=\\\"last bid R036; exclusivity R041\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"by 09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Dropped by target\\\", round=4, type_=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity - Party B was live when exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona was executed on 09/24/2013 (last proposal 09/18/2013, valued at $21.50 including options); the filing reports no notice to Party B. Decided by: Target; exit reason: Terms or process - the Special Committee cited the contingent/deferred options and the debt-financed structure as risks and preferred CSC/Pamplona's certainty.\\\",\\n count=1, decided=\\\"Target\\\", exitr=\\\"Terms or process\\\", obasis=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated execution: \\\" + Q(711, \\\"executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\\\") +\\n     \\\" Stated reasoning: \\\" + Q(703, \\\"the indication of interest submitted by Party B, including the Party B options, was on its face higher than the CSC/Pamplona proposal\\\", \\\"which did not require any third party financing.\\\") +\\n     \\\" No notice to Party B is reported. Convention: exclusivity execution closes live rivals.\\\",\\n src=CITE(711,698,703), main=711, review=\\\"Q4\\\", page=38,\\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,9,24), working=D(2013,9,24), basis=\\\"Relative only\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: decision day\\\",\\n related=\\\"last bid R037; exclusivity R041\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"09/25/2013-10/07/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Information access changed\\\", round=4, type_=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Once selected: CSC and Pamplona granted full access to the electronic data site and to certain members of management (previously limited as strategic bidders, with customer data withheld) and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence; confirmatory business-diligence meeting 10/01/2013. Access rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(712, \\\"Also during this time, CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Timing: the passage sits between the 09/25/2013 initial merger-agreement draft and the 10/07/2013 Special Committee meeting; period start assigned as the Working date.\\\",\\n src=CITE(712,716), main=712, review=\\\"Q1\\\", page=38, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,9,25), dto=D(2013,10,7), working=D(2013,9,25), basis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=\\\"earlier limited access R025; confirmatory diligence meeting R045 note\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"by 10/07/2013\\\", who=\\\"Moab (with CSC/Pamplona)\\\", what=\\\"Material process update\\\", round=4, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Rollover resolved: after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona beginning 09/23/2013 (facilitated by BofA Merrill Lynch), it was determined that Moab would not roll over any Moab shares in the transaction; reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013. Moab later signed a voting agreement at signing (R048). Rollover rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(718, \\\"Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Origin: \\\" + Q(712, \\\"Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Date: the determination is reported only as made by this meeting; upper bound taken as the Working date.\\\",\\n src=CITE(709,712,718), main=718, review=\\\"Q8\\\", page=39, count=None,\\n dfrom=None, dto=D(2013,10,7), working=D(2013,10,7), basis=\\\"Relative only\\\", method=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=\\\"denial R014; voting agreement at signing R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"10/12/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona (with Mac-Gray)\\\", what=\\\"Exclusivity changed\\\", round=4, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Extended: exclusivity was due to expire 5:00 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013; Kirkland requested an extension on CSC/Pamplona's behalf; the Special Committee authorized it on 10/09/2013 and again on 10/11/2013 (conditioned on a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, approximately 3.2% of total equity value) and the parties executed a letter agreement on 10/12/2013 extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013; the fee was agreed at $11 million on 10/11/2013. Exclusivity rows carry no Count.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(731, \\\"On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Authorization: \\\" + Q(725, \\\"Kirkland had requested on behalf of CSC/Pamplona that the exclusivity agreement, due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, be extended\\\", \\\"to extend exclusivity to October 15, 2013.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Condition: \\\" + Q(726, \\\"authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, which represented approximately 3.2% of the total equity value of the transaction.\\\"),\\n src=CITE(725,726,727,731), main=731, review=\\\"Q2\\\", page=41, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,10,12), dto=D(2013,10,12), working=D(2013,10,12), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"extends R041; fee history part of R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"10/14/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray; Spin Holdco Inc.; CSC Fenway, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.\\\", what=\\\"Merger agreement signed\\\", round=4, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Signed definitive merger agreement: CSC Fenway, Inc. (Merger Subsidiary) merges into Mac-Gray, which survives as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Spin Holdco Inc. (Parent); each outstanding share converted into $21.25 in cash (all-cash; no financing condition). Pamplona commitment letter delivered ($594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P.; Pamplona jointly and severally liable with the Buyer Entities for breaches, its damages liability capped at $50 million, Buyer Entities unlimited). $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee / $15 million Parent termination fee. Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement; the MacDonald and family voting agreements became effective; stockholders entering voting agreements held approximately 15% of shares at the 11/27/2013 record date. End date 03/31/2014 (extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains); completion expected in the first half of 2014 (not observed in the filing). Signing is not an extra bid, so price/formality/condition cells are blank.\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(736, \\\"Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Terms: \\\" + Q(216, \\\"each outstanding share of Mac-Gray common stock\\\", \\\"converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(232, \\\"Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital\\\", \\\"Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(309, \\\"Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances\\\", \\\"Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(322, \\\"the stockholders of Mac-Gray that entered into the voting agreements collectively owned approximately 15% of the Mac-Gray common stock entitled to vote at the special meeting.\\\") +\\n     \\\" See X-001/X-002/X-005/X-016/X-028/X-029 for party and agreement definitions.\\\",\\n src=CITE(734,736,173,215,216,232,282,309,312,322,1085,1101,1103), main=736, review=None, page=41, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,10,14), dto=D(2013,10,14), working=D(2013,10,14), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"concludes R040/R041/R042; announcement R049\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\\nrow(\\n when=\\\"10/15/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.\\\", what=\\\"Merger announced\\\", round=4, type_=None,\\n terms=\\\"Joint announcement by Mac-Gray and CSC before the U.S. stock markets opened. Post-signing status per the proxy: no competing proposal, go-shop or agreement termination disclosed; HSR waiting period expired 11/27/2013; merger litigation filed 11/21/2013 (see Summary; regulatory and litigation items are not separate ledger rows).\\\",\\n why=\\\"Stated: \\\" + Q(737, \\\"On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement.\\\") +\\n     \\\" Post-signing: \\\" + Q(324, \\\"While early termination was not granted, the waiting period expired on November 27, 2013.\\\") +\\n     \\\" \\\" + Q(1540, \\\"On November 21, 2013, a putative class action lawsuit was filed\\\", \\\"captioned Star Partners Fund v. Bullock, et al. , Civ. 13-5067.\\\"),\\n src=CITE(737,324,1538,1540), main=737, review=None, page=41, count=None,\\n dfrom=D(2013,10,15), dto=D(2013,10,15), working=D(2013,10,15), basis=\\\"Reported day\\\", method=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=\\\"follows R048\\\", deal=\\\"Mac-Gray\\\")\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/ledger_rows.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824802489,"end":1789824861584}}}}
