 action was filed 11/21/2013.\")\n s_head(\"2. Deal facts\")\n s_pair(\"Target\", \"Mac-Gray Corporation (Delaware; NYSE-listed; Waltham, Massachusetts), second largest U.S. laundry facilities management contractor. [X-002]\")\n s_pair(\"Focal acquirer and type\", \"CSC/Pamplona - the acquisition unit of CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. (operating acquirer; the filing calls Party A and CSC/Pamplona its two 'strategic bidders') with equity capital committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P., part of Pamplona Capital Management, which bought CSC in May 2013. Acquisition chain: Parent = Spin Holdco Inc. (wholly owned by CSC); Merger Subsidiary = CSC Fenway, Inc.; Holdings = CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc. Type = Strategic (operating-company acquisition role); sponsor ownership and sponsor financing do not make it Financial, and it is not Mixed. [P-026, P-027, X-001, X-003, X-004, X-005, X-006]\")\n-s_pair(\"Agreed consideration\", \"$21.25 per share in cash, without interest; all-cash; all outstanding shares converted at the effective time; no financing condition. Cash at closing: $21.25 per share. [X-009, X-010, X-013, X-029]\")\n-s_pair(\"Signing / announcement / completion\", \"Merger agreement signed 10/14/2013; jointly announced 10/15/2013 before market open; completion expected in the first half of 2014 and NOT observed in the filing (no closed-transaction row). End date 03/31/2014, extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains. [P-101, P-102, X-016, X-028]\")\n-s_pair(\"Filing identity\", \"DEFM14A, Mac-Gray Corporation, filed 12/04/2013; source file raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm; Background of the Merger at printed pages 27-41; record date 11/27/2013; special meeting 01/08/2014 at 10:00 a.m. Boston. [X-007, X-008]\")\n-s_pair(\"Market benchmarks (dates)\", \"Unaffected reference close $14.72 on 10/11/2013 (last trading day before board approval); 52-week high $15.61 for the period ending 10/11/2013; market close $21.30 on 11/27/2013. Agreed price represents approximately 36% premium to the 52-week high and approximately 44% to the 10/11/2013 close. [X-010, X-011, X-012, X-027]\")\n-s_pair(\"Shares and ownership\", \"14,758,306 shares outstanding and entitled to vote as of 11/27/2013; voting agreements covered approximately 15% of shares (2,697,484 shares per the 10/23/2013 Schedule 13D, beneficial ownership disclaimed by Parent, Merger Subsidiary, Holdings, CSC, Pamplona and Pamplona Capital Management entities). Moab held approximately 9% in June 2013. [X-007, X-019, X-030]\")\n+s_pair(\"Agreed consideration\", \"$21.25 per share in cash, without interest; all-cash; all outstanding shares converted at the effective time; no financing condition. Cash at closing: $21.25 per share. [X-009, X-013, X-030]\")\n+s_pair(\"Signing / announcement / completion\", \"Merger agreement signed 10/14/2013; jointly announced 10/15/2013 before market open; completion expected in the first half of 2014 and NOT observed in the filing (no closed-transaction row). End date 03/31/2014, extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains. [P-087, P-088, X-016, X-029]\")\n+s_pair(\"Filing identity\", \"DEFM14A, Mac-Gray Corporation, filed 12/04/2013; source file raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm; Background of the Merger at printed pages 27-41; record date 11/27/2013; special meeting 01/08/2014 at 10:00 a.m. Boston. [X-007, X-032]\")\n+s_pair(\"Market benchmarks (dates)\", \"Unaffected reference close $14.72 on 10/11/2013 (last trading day before board approval); 52-week high $15.61 for the period ending 10/11/2013; market close $21.30 on 11/27/2013. Agreed price represents approximately 36% premium to the 52-week high and approximately 44% to the 10/11/2013 close. [X-010, X-011, X-012, X-028]\")\n+s_pair(\"Shares and ownership\", \"14,758,306 shares outstanding and entitled to vote as of 11/27/2013; voting agreements covered approximately 15% of shares entitled to vote as of that date [X-019]; the related Sch