{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825168068,"sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e4ade8001KvctGDihh0yb25","sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","messageID":"msg_0b9e4a4c8001lvnxUNJCfL5O9U","type":"tool","id":"call_00_Dwsv2xi18LwAVJmgMsfH9721","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"  \"Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R022 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders'); the 08/27 letter only communicated the deadline. R3 is the target's first request for final indications (R033 quote). R4 applies the 'moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders' trigger; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not open a round. Sources: P-021 (R009), P-038/P-039 (R022), P-056 (R033), P-068 (R041-R042).\",","oldString":"  \"Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R021 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders'); the 08/27 letter only communicated the deadline. R3 is the target's first request for final indications (R032 quote). R4 applies the 'moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders' trigger; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not open a round. Sources: P-028 (R009), P-046/P-047 (R022), P-055 (R033), P-073 (R041-R042).\",","path":"/tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py"},"output":"Edited /tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"/tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py","patch":"Index: /tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py\n+++ /tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py\n@@ -343,9 +343,9 @@\n \n QUESTIONS = [\n  (\"Q1\", \"Process and round map; inferred starts; rejected boundary candidates\",\n   \"Keep one process and the four rounds as built: R1 06/24/2013 (sale decision/50-party solicitation; rejected anchors R008 and R012); R2 07/25/2013 (staged access and revised-IOI stage; rejected alternative R026, the 08/27/2013 letter); R3 09/11/2013 (first final-indications request; Announced as final); R4 09/24/2013 (executed exclusivity and definitive negotiation; Inferred final; alternative = fold into R3). Treat the 2011-2012 Discussions as context, not a second process.\",\n-  \"Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R021 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders'); the 08/27 letter only communicated the deadline. R3 is the target's first request for final indications (R032 quote). R4 applies the 'moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders' trigger; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not open a round. Sources: P-028 (R009), P-046/P-047 (R022), P-055 (R033), P-073 (R041-R042).\",\n+  \"Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R022 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders'); the 08/27 letter only communicated the deadline. R3 is the target's first request for final indications (R033 quote). R4 applies the 'moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders' trigger; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not open a round. Sources: P-021 (R009), P-038/P-039 (R022), P-056 (R033), P-068 (R041-R042).\",\n   \"R008, R009, R012, R022, R026, R033, R040, R041, R042; rounds/finality fields on R009/R022/R033/R042\",\n   \"Dating R2 at 08/27 moves the start of the staged-access stage and its access row (R025); merging R4 into R3 would put exclusivity, the two closures and signing in R3 and delete the Inferred-final row; treating R1 as opening at the 06/21 proposal would pull Party A's bid out of round 0.\",\n   \"Pending\", None),\n  (\"Q2\", \"Deadline changes and elapsed-deadline treatments\",\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited /tmp/opencode/make_workbook.py (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"  \\\"Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R022 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders'); the 08/27 letter only communicated the deadline. R3 is the target's first request for final indications (R033 quote). R4 applies the 'moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders' trigger; exclusivity inside an already-established final negot