t strategic alternatives on 05/09/2013. An exploration authorization, not the sale-process launch (see R009).\n9: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n10: WHY: Stated: “authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities that might be available to Mac-Gray, including opportunities with another strategic party, whom we refer to as Party A, in the laundry facilities management industry” Qualification: the Board only “determined to further consider Mac-Gray's strategic alternatives at its meeting scheduled for May 9, 2013.” Counting: no tally contribution (process-wide decision row).\n11: SOURCE: P-004 | PAGE: 27 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: followed by R003 contact and R009 sale-process opening\n12: \n13: ===== R003 | Contact | round 0 | 04/08/2013 | Party A =====\n14: TERMS: Direction: target-initiated (BofA Merrill Lynch telephoned, as instructed by the Board). First sale-related contact; Party A indicated it might consider a business combination with Mac-Gray. Pre-process (round 0).\n15: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: 1\n16: WHY: Stated: “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray.” Count 1 = the newly represented bidder unit for the contact step; the same bidder's 06/21/2013 Bid row (R008) adds no second contact count.\n17: SOURCE: P-005 | PAGE: 27 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: same bidder later bids (R008) and signs NDA (R024)\n18: \n19: ===== R004 | Material process update | round 0 | 05/09/2013 | Mac-Gray Board of Directors =====\n20: TERMS: Board reviewed the sale-process option (risks/benefits, potential disruption, leak risk, disclosure to competitors) alongside standalone alternatives; formed a Transaction Committee (Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust) to administer the strategic-alternatives review and recommend a financial adviser; deferred a decision to the next meeting.\n21: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n22: WHY: Stated: “the Board formed a transaction committee at this meeting, which we refer to as the Transaction Committee, and appointed Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust, both independent directors, to serve as its members.” No sale decision or outreach yet; recorded because the governance step structures the process that follows.\n23: SOURCE: P-009; P-006 | PAGE: 28 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: leads to adviser selection (R006) and sale decision (R009)\n24: \n25: ===== R005 | Adviser ended | round 0 | 05/15/2013 | BofA Merrill Lynch =====\n26: TERMS: Termination of the 2011-2012 Discussions engagement: the Transaction Committee determined on 05/14/2013 to terminate; Mac-Gray sent the termination letter 05/15/2013. Not a termination of the sale process (which had not begun).\n27: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n28: WHY: Stated: “On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions.” Determination: “the Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch's engagement letter entered into for purposes of the 2011-2012 Discussions.” Adviser rows carry no Count.\n29: SOURCE: P-012; P-011 | PAGE: 29 | REVIEW: Q8 | RELATED: ends the R001 mandate; new mandate in R006\n30: \n31: ===== R006 | Adviser engaged | round 0 | 05/30/2013 | BofA Merrill Lynch =====\n32: TERMS: Mac-Gray's financial advisor for the strategic-alternatives review and sale process; Board unanimously approved the engagement on 05/30/2013; engagement letter entered 05/31/2013; BofA agreed not to engage as a possible source of new acquisition financing for any potential buyer without Mac-Gray's prior written consent. Three nationally recognized banks were invited to submit proposals; the other two presented 05/29/2013.\n33: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n34: WHY: Stated: “the Board unanimously approved the engagement of BofA Merrill Lynch on the terms discussed at 