cted boundary candidate R041/R042\n198: \n199: ===== R034 | Deadline | round 3 | 09/18/2013 | Mac-Gray / BofA Merrill Lynch =====\n200: TERMS: Scheduled due date for final indications of interest. CSC/Pamplona, Party A and Party B responded on the date; Party C did not. The Special Committee took its next step on 09/19/2013, authorizing exclusive negotiation with CSC/Pamplona on the bids in hand: Enforced.\n201: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n202: WHY: Stated: “On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share” and the Special Committee meeting of 09/19/2013: “On September 19, 2013, the Special Committee held an in-person meeting.” Convention: treatment Enforced - the date passed with no extension and no late acceptance, and the target took its next step (selection/exclusivity) on the bids in hand. Party C's non-response is recorded at R038.\n203: SOURCE: P-059; P-056; P-060 | PAGE: 36 | REVIEW: Q2 | RELATED: submissions R035, R036, R037; non-submission R038\n204: \n205: ===== R035 | Bid | round 3 | 09/18/2013 | CSC/Pamplona =====\n206: TERMS: All-cash proposal at $20.75 per share; Pamplona's 100% capital commitment reiterated; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Formality: Formal (signal 2 - response on the requested basis to the final-indications solicitation); Conditions: Light (committed financing, no diligence condition stated); diligence still open.\n207: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | COUNT: 1\n208: WHY: Stated: “CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks.” Convention: Formality signal 2 despite the non-binding IOI form; Conditions Light. Count 1 = first R3 submission by this unit.\n209: SOURCE: P-059 | PAGE: 36 | REVIEW: Q5; Q6 | RELATED: revises R028; revised to last-and-best R040\n210: \n211: ===== R036 | Bid reaffirmed | round 3 | 09/18/2013 | Party A =====\n212: TERMS: Telephone confirmation that the $18.00-$19.00 indication stood as Party A's best and final offer; no improvement. Price carried forward from R030. Formality: Formal (signal 2 - response in the best-and-final stage; borderline, flagged Q5). Conditions reassessed: financing not committed; diligence open.\n213: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Heavy | COUNT: 1\n214: WHY: Stated: “Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.” Convention: recorded as Bid reaffirmed (actual bidder confirmation that its offer stands); price carried forward with origin Carried forward, not restated. Count 1 - first reaffirmation by this unit in round 3.\n215: SOURCE: P-059 | PAGE: 36 | REVIEW: Q5; Q6 | RELATED: reaffirms R030; closed R043\n216: \n217: ===== R037 | Bid | round 3 | 09/18/2013 | Party B =====\n218: TERMS: Revised indication of interest that Party B valued at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash paid at closing plus options the bidder valued at $2.50 (options for 10% of new equity, strike at initial cost basis, vesting over five years on base-case management projections excluding future acquisitions). Cash component below CSC/Pamplona's $20.75; total above it but contingent/deferred; financing remained affiliated-fund equity plus third-party debt without a firm commitment. Price cells show the cash component and the bidder's stated total valuation (package, not a submitted range) - flagged Q7.\n219: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Heavy | COUNT: 1\n220: WHY: Stated: “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis.” “Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.” Formality: signal 2 response to the final solicitation; Conditions: no firm financing commitment (Heavy); risk view in R039/R044. Count 1 = first R3 submission by this unit.\n221: SOURCE: P-059; P-061; P-062 | PAGE: 36 | REVIEW: Q5; Q6; Q7 | RELATED: revises R029; closed R044\n222: \n223: ===== R038 | Did not submit | round 3 | by 09/18/2013 | Party C =====\n224: TERMS: Did not submit a revised indication or reiterate its prior $16.00-$17.00 indication at the final-indications solicitation and gave no reasons (the filing states the fact, not the cause); no notice, discouragement or withdrawal is reported. Decided by Unknown; exit reason Not stated. Count 1 = this unit.\n225: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: 1\n226: WHY: Stated: “Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith.” Reported again: “reported that Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest.” Convention: non-submission is not a withdrawal and agency is not inferred from silence; recorded at the due date.\n227: SOURCE: P-059; P-060 | PAGE: 36 | REVIEW: Q4 | RELATED: last bid R031; next recorded activity none\n228: \n229: ===== R039 | Target decision | round 3 | 09/19/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee =====\n230: TERMS: Preferred-bidder and exclusivity decision: the Special Committee concluded CSC/Pamplona's revised indication had the potential to deliver the most value with greater certainty and less risk than the alternatives (Party B's options contingent/deferred and Party B reliant on third-party debt; Party A's lower best-and-final); expected CSC/Pamplona to be able to increase above $20.75 given synergies; authorized the Transaction Committee to tell CSC/Pamplona Mac-Gray was prepared to move to exclusivity at $21.25 per share and to negotiate exclusivity terms; Mr. MacDonald said he would be supportive at $21.25. Not a round opening (a selection inside round 3).\n231: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n232: WHY: Stated: “the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications.” “authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share” “Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share.” Convention: no Count on a process-wide decision.\n233: SOURCE: P-062; P-060; P-061 | PAGE: 37 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: follows R034; leads to R040, R041\n234: \n235: ===== R040 | Bid | round 3 | 09/21/2013 | CSC/Pamplona =====\n236: TERMS: Increase to $21.25 per share all cash as a last and best offer, provided Mac-Gray agree to a two-week exclusive negotiation; CSC/Pamplona also requested a voting agreement covering shares of Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family. Target proposed the price point on the same call; price revision solicited by the target after the due date belongs to the round's continuing negotiation. Count 0: same bidder and round as R035 - this is a revision, not a new unit.\n237: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | COUNT: 0\n238: WHY: Stated: “the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations. The representative of CSC/Pamplona also requested that shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned beneficially and of record by Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family be subject to a customary voting agreement” Formality: carried forward from the formal R035 submission (price confirmation in final negotiation). Conditions: committed financing, no diligence condition stated (Light); diligence open.\n239: SOURCE: P-063; P-064 | PAGE: 37 | REVIEW: Q5; Q6 | RELATED: revises R035; basis of R041 and R048; voting-agreement request part of R048\n240: \n241: ===== R041 | Exclusivity changed | round 4 | 09/24/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (with Mac-Gray) =====\n242: TERMS: Granted: exclusive negotiations until 5:00 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to CSC and Pamplona not adversely changing the final proposal terms, which included: no financing contingency; Pamplona committed to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing; a $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance is not obtained; certain post-signing covenants. Requested by CSC/Pamplona on 09/09 and 09/18; Special Committee authorized entering exclusivity on 09/23/2013 after CSC/Pamplona confirmed $21.25 as last and best on 09/21/2013. Dropped every other live bidder on the execution date (R043, R044).\n243: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n244: WHY: Stated: “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.” Terms: “the inclusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained, which we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee” and “committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, which, together with the all-cash per share purchase price of $21.25, we refer to as the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.” Exclusivity rows carry no Count.\n245: SOURCE: P-068; P-064; P-065; P-066; P-067 | PAGE: 38 | REVIEW: Q2; Q4 | RELATED: follows R040; opened R042; drops R043, R044; extended R047; basis of R048\n246: \n247: ===== R042 | Round opened | round 4 | 09/24/2013 | CSC/Pamplona =====\n248: TERMS: Round 4: exclusive negotiation and definitive-agreement stage with the selected bidder CSC/Pamplona, beginning with the executed exclusivity agreement; single-bidder stage (no organized competing solicitation). Round finality: Inferred final - the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder without a further finality announcement. Alternative boundary treatment (fold this stage into round 3) is listed in Q1.\n249: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n250: WHY: Stated: “executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” Next steps: “Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement.” Convention: a round can open when the target moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not be a new round.\n251: SOURCE: P-068; P-069 | PAGE: 38 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: opens with R041; signed R048\n252: \n253: ===== R043 | Dropped by target | round 4 | by 09/24/2013 | Party A =====\n254: TERMS: Inferred: exclusivity — Party A was live when the target executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013 (last bid reaffirmed 09/18/2013 as best and final); the filing reports no notice to Party A. Decided by: Target; exit reason: Would not improve earlier offer (asked for final indications and declined to improve on $18.00-$19.00).\n255: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: 1\n256: WHY: Stated execution: “CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” Party A's last act: “Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.” No notice to Party A is reported. Convention: executing exclusivity with one bidder closes every other bidder still live in the stage; the reason preserves the informative stated constraint without changing agency.\n257: SOURCE: P-068; P-059 | PAGE: 38 | REVIEW: Q4 | RELATED: last bid R036; exclusivity R041\n258: \n259: ===== R044 | Dropped by target | round 4 | by 09/24/2013 | Party B =====\n260: TERMS: Inferred: exclusivity — Party B was live when exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona was executed on 09/24/2013 (last proposal 09/18/2013, valued at $21.50 including options); the filing reports no notice to Party B. Decided by: Target; exit reason: Terms or process - the Special Committee cited the contingent/deferred options and the debt-financed structure as risks and preferred CSC/Pamplona's certainty.\n261: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: 1\n262: WHY: Stated execution: “executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” Stated reasoning: “the indication of interest submitted by Party B, including the Party B options, was on its face higher than the CSC/Pamplona proposal but further discussed the risks and complexities involved with measuring and achieving the performance required to vest the Party B options. The Special Committee also noted that Party B would likely be financing the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt capital, which would involve more risk than the Pamplona-funded CSC/Pamplona proposal, which did not require any third party financing.” No notice to Party B is reported. Convention: exclusivity execution closes live rivals.\n263: SOURCE: P-068; P-059; P-062 | PAGE: 38 | REVIEW: Q4 | RELATED: last bid R037; exclusivity R041\n264: \n265: ===== R045 | Information access changed | round 4 | 09/25/2013-10/07/2013 | CSC/Pamplona =====\n266: TERMS: Once selected: CSC and Pamplona granted full access to the electronic data site and to certain members of management (previously limited as strategic bidders, with customer data withheld) and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence; confirmatory business-diligence meeting 10/01/2013. Access rows carry no Count.\n267: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n268: WHY: Stated: “Also during this time, CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray.” Timing: the passage sits between the 09/25/2013 initial merger-agreement draft and the 10/07/2013 Special Committee meeting; period start assigned as the Working date.\n269: SOURCE: P-069; P-071 | PAGE: 38 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: earlier limited access R025; confirmatory diligence meeting R045 note\n270: \n271: ===== R046 | Material process update | round 4 | by 10/07/2013 | Moab (with CSC/Pamplona) =====\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 272]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825205605,"end":1789825205703}}}}
