{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825212970,"sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e561ac001LIPCYYlhiht96Q","sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","messageID":"msg_0b9e545d8001xpzq3rZlH32f8U","type":"tool","id":"call_00_XsVvXvrE5eiEFKcwqevj4591","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"offset":272,"path":"/tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt, lines 272-294\n272: TERMS: Rollover resolved: after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona beginning 09/23/2013 (facilitated by BofA Merrill Lynch), it was determined that Moab would not roll over any Moab shares in the transaction; reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013. Moab later signed a voting agreement at signing (R048). Rollover rows carry no Count.\n273: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n274: WHY: Stated: “Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.” Origin: “Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares.” Date: the determination is reported only as made by this meeting; upper bound taken as the Working date.\n275: SOURCE: P-073; P-066; P-069 | PAGE: 39 | REVIEW: Q8 | RELATED: denial R014; voting agreement at signing R048\n276: \n277: ===== R047 | Exclusivity changed | round 4 | 10/12/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (with Mac-Gray) =====\n278: TERMS: Extended: exclusivity was due to expire 5:00 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013; Kirkland requested an extension on CSC/Pamplona's behalf; the Special Committee authorized it on 10/09/2013 and again on 10/11/2013 (conditioned on a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, approximately 3.2% of total equity value) and the parties executed a letter agreement on 10/12/2013 extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013; the fee was agreed at $11 million on 10/11/2013. Exclusivity rows carry no Count.\n279: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n280: WHY: Stated: “On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013.” Authorization: “Kirkland had requested on behalf of CSC/Pamplona that the exclusivity agreement, due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, be extended to allow for continued negotiations of these open issues. After discussion, the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within certain parameters and in connection therewith to extend exclusivity to October 15, 2013.” Condition: “authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million, which represented approximately 3.2% of the total equity value of the transaction.”\n281: SOURCE: P-082; P-078; P-079; P-080 | PAGE: 41 | REVIEW: Q2 | RELATED: extends R041; fee history part of R048\n282: \n283: ===== R048 | Merger agreement signed | round 4 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray; Spin Holdco Inc.; CSC Fenway, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. =====\n284: TERMS: Signed definitive merger agreement: CSC Fenway, Inc. (Merger Subsidiary) merges into Mac-Gray, which survives as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Spin Holdco Inc. (Parent); each outstanding share converted into $21.25 in cash (all-cash; no financing condition). Pamplona commitment letter delivered ($594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P.; Pamplona jointly and severally liable with the Buyer Entities for breaches, its damages liability capped at $50 million, Buyer Entities unlimited). $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee / $15 million Parent termination fee. Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement; the MacDonald and family voting agreements became effective; stockholders entering voting agreements held approximately 15% of shares at the 11/27/2013 record date. End date 03/31/2014 (extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains); completion expected in the first half of 2014 (not observed in the filing). Signing is not an extra bid, so price/formality/condition cells are blank.\n285: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n286: WHY: Stated: “Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective.” Terms: “each outstanding share of Mac-Gray common stock (other than shares held in treasury or held by the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary (or their subsidiaries) or shares as to which dissenters' rights have been perfected and not withdrawn or lost) will be automatically converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes” “Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment amount and which is committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013” “Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances, which we refer to as the Mac-Gray termination fee. Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances, which we refer to as the Parent termination fee.” “the stockholders of Mac-Gray that entered into the voting agreements collectively owned approximately 15% of the Mac-Gray common stock entitled to vote at the special meeting.” Party-chain and agreement definitions: X-001, X-004 to X-006; end date X-016; termination fees X-017; voting agreements X-018, X-019; expected completion X-029; consideration X-030.\n287: SOURCE: P-087; P-085; X-001; X-008; X-009; X-013; X-016; X-017; X-018; X-019; X-021; X-029; X-030 | PAGE: 41 | REVIEW:  | RELATED: concludes R040/R041/R042; announcement R049\n288: \n289: ===== R049 | Merger announced | round 4 | 10/15/2013 | Mac-Gray; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. =====\n290: TERMS: Joint announcement by Mac-Gray and CSC before the U.S. stock markets opened. The proxy discloses no competing proposal, go-shop or agreement termination between signing and the 12/04/2013 proxy date; regulatory clearances and related litigation are reported in the Summary only.\n291: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n292: WHY: Stated: “On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement.” Post-signing: the proxy discloses no competing proposal, go-shop or agreement termination; see Summary for the single regulatory-clearance and litigation line.\n293: SOURCE: P-088 | PAGE: 41 | REVIEW:  | RELATED: follows R048\n294: ","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt, lines 272-294\n272: TERMS: Rollover resolved: after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona beginning 09/23/2013 (facilitated by BofA Merrill Lynch), it was determined that Moab would not roll over any Moab shares in the transaction; reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013. Moab later signed a voting agreement at signing (R048). Rollover rows carry no Count.\n273: FORMALITY:  | CONDITIONS:  | COUNT: \n274: WHY: Stated: “Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.” Origin: “Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares.” Date: the determination is reported only as made 