{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825220558,"sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e57f76001l8bwyY2YayLGGx","sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","messageID":"msg_0b9e5779c001TCqsNei7VWi4at","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_7B6FQIvuRxNkH0NJkQIs5499","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/summary_dump.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/summary_dump.txt, lines 1-107\n1: [1] A: MAC-GRAY / CSC SERVICEWORKS - DEAL LEDGER SUMMARY\n2: [2] A: 1. Status and commercial account\n3: [3] A: AI status\n4:       B: AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction: revision of 19 September 2026 (short form).\n5: [4] A: Source coverage\n6:       B: DEFM14A filed 12/04/2013; work only from this filing and the instruction. Complete Background of the Merger selected and reproduced on the Source text sheet in source order (P-001 to P-088, printed pages 27-41); other filing passages used are X-001 to X-031. Source text is HTML-derived: whitespace normalized, page-break artifacts and repeated 'Table of Contents' headers removed; paragraphs split by printed page breaks appear as separate '(cont.)' rows; no wording changes. Local source filename: raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm.\n7: [5] A: Commercial account\n8:       B: Initiation: after CSC's sale to Pamplona closed in May 2013, Mac-Gray's board explored strategic alternatives, and on June 24, 2013 the Special Committee concluded a sale was in stockholders' best interests and authorized its banker to solicit 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial); Party A had already made an unsolicited $17.00-$19.00 all-cash proposal on June 21, 2013. Competition: four bidder units - Party A (strategic), Party B and Party C (unnamed financial sponsors) and CSC/Pamplona (operating buyer CSC funded by sponsor Pamplona) - were individually recorded among 20 NDA signers and advanced through management meetings and two rounds of revised and final indications, while 16 other signers never submitted. Price path: CSC/Pamplona moved $18.50 (07/23) to $19.50 (09/09) to $20.75 (09/18) and to $21.25 last and best (09/21); Party B peaked at a $21.50-valued package ($19.00 cash plus options) whose cash and certainty lagged; Party A held at $18.00-$19.00 as best and final; Party C stopped at $16.00-$17.00 and did not respond to the final solicitation. Selection: on 09/19 the Special Committee found CSC/Pamplona's proposal most valuable with greater certainty and authorized exclusivity at $21.25; exclusivity was executed 09/24/2013 (to 5 p.m. ET 10/12, extended to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15) with a $15 million reverse termination fee and no financing contingency, Pamplona committed $594 million, and Moab and Mr. MacDonald did not roll over shares. Signing and publicity: the merger agreement was signed 10/14/2013 and announced 10/15/2013; voting agreements covered about 15% of shares; the proxy shows no competing proposal or go-shop and sets the special meeting for 01/08/2014. Observed outcome: signed, not closed - completion expected in the first half of 2014, the HSR waiting period expired 11/27/2013, and a putative class action was filed 11/21/2013.\n9: [6] A: 2. Deal facts\n10: [7] A: Target\n11:       B: Mac-Gray Corporation (Delaware; NYSE-listed; Waltham, Massachusetts), second largest U.S. laundry facilities management contractor. [X-002]\n12: [8] A: Focal acquirer and type\n13:       B: CSC/Pamplona - the acquisition unit of CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. (operating acquirer; the filing calls Party A and CSC/Pamplona its two 'strategic bidders') with equity capital committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P., part of Pamplona Capital Management, which bought CSC in May 2013. Acquisition chain: Parent = Spin Holdco Inc. (wholly owned by CSC); Merger Subsidiary = CSC Fenway, Inc.; Holdings = CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc. Type = Strategic (operating-company acquisition role); sponsor ownership and sponsor financing do not make it Financial, and it is not Mixed. [P-026, P-027, X-001, X-003, X-004, X-005, X-006]\n14: [9] A: Agreed consideration\n15:       B: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest; all-cash; all outstanding shares converted at the effective time; no financing condition. Cash at closing: $21.25 per share. [X-009, X-013, X-030]\n16: [10] A: Signing / announcement / completion\n17:       B: Merger agreement signed 10/14/2013; jointly announced 10/15/2013 before market open; completion expected in the first half of 2014 and NOT observed in the filing (no closed-transaction row). End date 03/31/2014, extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains. [P-087, P-088, X-016, X-029]\n18: [11] A: Filing identity\n19:       B: DEFM14A, Mac-Gray Corporation, filed 12/04/2013; source file raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm; Background of the Merger at printed pages 27-41; record date 11/27/2013; special meeting 01/08/2014 at 10:00 a.m. Boston. [X-007, X-032]\n20: [12] A: Market benchmarks (dates)\n21:       B: Unaffected reference close $14.72 on 10/11/2013 (last trading day before board approval); 52-week high $15.61 for the period ending 10/11/2013; market close $21.30 on 11/27/2013. Agreed price represents approximately 36% premium to the 52-week high and approximately 44% to the 10/11/2013 close. [X-010, X-011, X-012, X-028]\n22: [13] A: Shares and ownership\n23:       B: 14,758,306 shares outstanding and entitled to vote as of 11/27/2013; voting agreements covered approximately 15% of shares entitled to vote as of that date [X-019]; the related Schedule 13D filed 10/23/2013 reported deemed beneficial ownership of 2,697,484 shares by Parent, Merger Subsidiary, Holdings, CSC, Pamplona and Pamplona Capital Management entities, all disclaimed [X-030]. Moab held approximately 9% in June 2013 [P-019].\n24: [14] A: Financing\n25:       B: $594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. under a commitment letter dated 10/14/2013 for closing funding and related obligations; no financing condition to closing; Pamplona and the Buyer Entities jointly and severally liable for breaches with Pamplona's damages liability capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited). [X-013, X-031]\n26: [15] A: Termination fees\n27:       B: $11 million payable by Mac-Gray (as finally agreed 10/11/2013; earlier proposals were $15 million and $10.5 million); $15 million Parent termination fee. Deal-protection terms are not separate ledger rows per instruction; the fee history appears in the Background (P-074 to P-081). [X-017]\n28: [16] A: Optional labelled calculation\n29:       B: Equity value at the record-date share count = 14,758,306 x $21.25 = formula below (calculation, not a filing assertion; the filing does not state a total equity value, and the termination-fee percentage statements imply larger totals of roughly $341-$350 million on a different share base). No net debt, option, RSU or dilution adjustments are assumed.\n30: [17] A: Equity value (optional; ledger input)\n31:       B: =14758306*21.25\n32: [18] A: None\n33:       B: Sources for inputs: X-007 (shares outstanding) and X-009 (price per share). Excluded from bid-count formulas; flagged as a derived calculation.\n34: [19] A: 3. Process and round map\n35: [20] A: Process map\n36:       B: One sale process (Process 1). Earlier context: the 2011-2012 Discussions were Mac-Gray's prospective acquisition of CSC, not a Mac-Gray sale process (no Process terminated/restarted rows). No separate post-signing stage opened: the proxy discloses no competing proposal, no go-shop and no agreement termination as of 12/04/2013.\n37: [21] A: Round 0 (pre-opening)\n38:       B: No organized round and no Round opened row. Party A contact 04/08/2013 (R003) and unsolicited pre-NDA proposal 06/21/2013 $17.00-$19.00 (R008), standing when round 1 began. Adviser and activist context rows (R001-R007).\n39: [22] A: Round 1 (R009, opens 06/24/2013)\n40:       B: R1 anchor: 06/24/2013 Special Committee decision to consider a sale and authorize solicitation of 50 parties; rejected candidate anchors R008 (06/21 proposal) and R012 (06/28 first NDA); first outreach-wave date not disclosed. Objective: initial outreach and preliminary IOIs. Participants: 50 parties approached (15 strategic, 35 financial); 20 NDA signers entered (R012, R013, R015, R016). Deadline 07/23/2013, treatment Late bids accepted (on-time CSC/Pamplona R018; Party B 07/24 R020; Party C 07/24-25 R021, R023). Finality Not final. Round bidders 4: CSC/Pamplona $18.50, Party B $17.00-$18.00, Party C $15.00-$17.00 (oral), plus Party A's standing $17.00-$19.00 from R008 (explicit inclusion). Ending: 16 residual signers closed as non-submitters (R019); four bidders advanced.\n41: [23] A: Round 2 (R022, opens 07/25/2013)\n42:       B: Objective: staged information access and management meetings, then revised indications. Participants: Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (R023 written IOI; NDA R024). Differential access row R025 (financial bidders broad data-site access; strategic bidders limited, customer data withheld). Deadline set 08/27/2013 for 09/09/2013 (R026); treatment Late bids accepted (CSC/Pamplona and Party B 09/09 R028-R029; Party A and Party C 09/10 R030-R031; reviewed 09/11). Finality Not final. Round bidders 4: CSC/Pamplona $19.50, Party B $18.50, Party A $18.00-$19.00, Party C $16.00-$17.00. Alternative anchor candidate (rejected): R026 (08/27 letter).\n43: [24] A: Round 3 (R033, opens 09/11/2013)\n44:       B: Objective: first request for final indications of interest, with possible short exclusive negotiation. Participants: the same four. Deadline 09/18/2013 (R034), treatment Enforced (target's next step 09/19). Finality Announced as final. Round bidders 3: CSC/Pamplona $20.75 (R035), Party B $21.50-valued package (R037), Party A reaffirmed $18.00-$19.00 best and final (R036); Party C did not submit (R038). Selection 09/19 (R039); final price $21.25 agreed 09/21 (R040).\n45: [25] A: Round 4 (R042, opens 09/24/2013)\n46:       B: Objective: exclusive negotiation and definitive agreement with selected bidder CSC/Pamplona, beginning on execution of the exclusivity agreement (R041). Participants: CSC/Pamplona only; Party A and Party B closed the same day by exclusivity (R043, R044). No bid-submission deadline; exclusivity expiry 5 p.m. ET 10/12/2013 was extended to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15/2013 (R047). Finality Inferred final. Signing R048 (10/14) and announcement R049 (10/15). Alternative treatment (fold into round 3) flagged in Q1.\n47: [26] A: Post-signing\n48:       B: No competing proposal, go-shop start/change or agreement termination is disclosed as of 12/04/2013. Regulatory: HSR filings 10/29/2013, early termination not granted, waiting period expired 11/27/2013 [X-022]. Litigation: putative class action filed 11/21/2013 [X-023]. These belong here, not as ledger rows.\n49: [27] A: 4. Participants and advisers\n50: [28] A: Party A (strategic; unnamed)\n51:       B: First observed 04/08/2013 contact (R003); pre-NDA proposal 06/21/2013 (R008); NDA 08/05/2013 (R024); revised indication 09/10/2013 (R030); best-and-final reaffirmation 09/18/2013 (R036); closed Dropped by target on 09/24/2013 by exclusivity (R043; inferred; exit reason Would not improve earlier offer). Type basis: laundry-industry strategic party, one of the filing's two named strategic bidders [P-034].\n52: [29] A: Party B (financial; unnamed)\n53:       B: First observed NDA 06/28/2013 (R012); IOIs 07/24, 09/09 and the $21.50-valued cash-plus-options proposal 09/18/2013 (R020, R029, R037); closed Dropped by target on 09/24/2013 by exclusivity (R044; inferred; exit reason Terms or process). Type basis: one of the 18 financial bidders, with affiliated-fund equity [P-034, P-052].\n54: [30] A: Party C (financial; unnamed)\n55:       B: First observed NDA 06/30/2013 (R013); oral and written IOIs 07/24-25 (R021, R023) and revised oral indication 09/10/2013 (R031); did not submit at the final-indications solicitation and gave no reasons; closed Did not submit on 09/18/2013 (R038; stated; agency Unknown). Type basis: one of the financial bidders [P-034].\n56: [31] A: CSC/Pamplona (strategic; winner)\n57:       B: First observed contact 06/28/2013 (R011); NDA 07/11/2013 (R015); bids 07/23 $18.50, 09/09 $19.50, 09/18 $20.75 and 09/21 $21.25 last and best (R018, R028, R035, R040); exclusivity 09/24/2013 (R041); signing 10/14/2013 (R048). No exit row (winner). Unit composition: CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. (operating acquirer) and Pamplona (equity capital commitment); Pamplona's funding is support, not a membership change or joint-bidder formation.\n58: [32] A: 16 residual NDA signers (financial)\n59:       B: Entered as residual cohort of 20 signers less the four recorded individually (R016; count 16); closed Did not submit by 07/23/2013 (R019; inferred residual; base assumes all 20 were eligible - flagged Q3).\n60: [33] A: Moab Partners, L.P. (shareholder, approximately 9%)\n61:       B: Not a bidder. Proxy contest and two directors elected 05/30/2013 (R007); rollover request denied 07/06/2013 (R014) and resolved without a rollover by 10/07/2013 (R046); voting agreement at signing (R048).\n62: [34] A: Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. (CEO; significant holder)\n63:       B: Not a bidder. Excluded from sale-process evaluation 06/24/2013 (R009); declined a share rollover 09/11/2013 and wanted a higher value (R032); supportive of $21.25 (R039); voting agreement effective at signing (R048).\n64: [35] A: Advisers\n65:       B: BofA Merrill Lynch (Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner & Smith Incorporated) - Mac-Gray's financial advisor: 2011-2012 Discussions engagement 10/23/2012 (R001), terminated 05/15/2013 (R005), re-engaged for the sale process by Board approval 05/30/2013 with engagement letter 05/31/2013 (R006); delivered the fairness opinion dated 10/14/2013 [X-027]. Goodwin Procter LLP - outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray (observed acting from 05/09/2013, R004; drafted the merger agreement and advised the Special Committee throughout). Kirkland & Ellis LLP - outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona from 09/25/2013 (R042 note). Clients are as stated by the filing; no unclear client affiliations identified.\n66: [36] A: 5. Counts and auction screen\n67: [37] A: NDA signers (ledger)\n68:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"NDA signed\")\n69: [38] A: None\n70:       B: Filing assertion: 20 (two strategic bidders - Party A and CSC/Pamplona - and 18 financial bidders, including Party B and Party C) [P-034]. Ledger = 4 individually recorded signers + 16 residual cohort = 20; reconciles exactly. Residual dates and eligibility are uncertain (Q3).\n71: [39] A: First sale-related contacts (ledger)\n72:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Contact\")\n73: [40] A: None\n74:       B: Filing process-level assertion: 50 parties approached (15 strategic, 35 financial) [P-032, P-033]. Only Party A (04/08/2013) and CSC/Pamplona (06/28/2013) are individually dated; the other contacts are not individually reported, so no exact reconciliation is claimed.\n75: [41] A: Round-1 round bidders (submissions)\n76:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,1,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,1,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid reaffirmed\")\n77: [42] A: None\n78:       B: Explicit inclusion: + 1 standing round-0 proposal (Party A, R008, whose Bid row sits in round 0 but who participated in round 1) = 4 round bidders. Units, not submissions or unique firms.\n79: [43] A: Round-2 round bidders\n80:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,2,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,2,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid reaffirmed\")\n81: [44] A: None\n82:       B: Four units: CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party A, Party C. Not a submission count (Party C has two rows in round 1 and one in round 2; revisions carry Count 0).\n83: [45] A: Round-3 round bidders\n84:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,3,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,3,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid reaffirmed\")\n85: [46] A: None\n86:       B: Three units (CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party A); Party C did not submit and is an outcome row (R038), not a round bidder. Round 4 has no bid rows: one unit continued in exclusive definitive negotiation.\n87: [47] A: Outcome tallies (affected units)\n88:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Dropped by target\")\n89: [48] A: None\n90:       B: Dropped by target = 2 units (Party A, Party B at 09/24). Did not submit: 16 residual at 07/23 (R019) + Party C at 09/18 (R038) = 17 units; formula above shows only the Dropped tally; totals are occurrences/affected units, not unique permanent exits. Winner CSC/Pamplona has no exit row.\n91: [49] A: Auction screen\n92:       B: Met: more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process - four units are individually recorded (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) among 20 signers total. Excluded: no lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements reported; no agreements expressly reused from an earlier attempt (the 2011-2012 Discussions produced no reused NDA).\n93: [50] A: Per-stage balance (participants)\n94:       B: R0: entrants 1 (Party A) - exits 0 = 1 live. R1: entrants +19 (16 cohort + Party B + Party C + CSC/Pamplona; Party A already in) = 20; exits -16 (residual non-submitters, R019) = 4. R2: exits 0 = 4. R3: exits -1 (Party C, R038) = 3. R4: exits -2 (Party A and Party B by exclusivity, R043-R044) = 1 = winner at signing (R048); no participant left open. Inferred share of exits: 18 of 19 (the 16 residual plus the two exclusivity drops); Party C's exit is stated. Counts are tally contributions, not population balances.\n95: [51] A: 6. Comparability and inputs\n96: [52] A: Other-scope proposals\n97:       B: None: every recorded proposal concerns acquisition of the whole company's equity. No segment, asset, minority or other-scope bids and no group price envelopes.\n98: [53] A: Unusual consideration\n99:       B: Party B's 09/18/2013 cash-plus-options package: $19.00 cash at closing plus options it valued at $2.50 per share (10% of new equity, strike at its initial cost basis, vesting over five years on base-case projections). Recorded as All cash = No; structured price cells show the cash component and the bidder's stated total ($19.00-$21.50) and are flagged as a package representation (Q7). No CVR or earnout in the signed deal.\n100: [54] A: Currency and units\n101:       B: All amounts USD per share; no currency conversion performed. Agreed consideration and all recorded bid prices are per share of Mac-Gray common stock.\n102: [55] A: Stated deal inputs\n103:       B: Shares outstanding 14,758,306 at 11/27/2013 [X-007]; market close $21.30 on 11/27/2013 [X-012]; unaffected close $14.72 and 52-week high $15.61 on 10/11/2013 [X-010, X-011, X-027]; $594 million Pamplona commitment [X-013, X-031]; $11 million / $15 million termination fees [X-017]; voting agreements approximately 15% [X-019, X-030]. No net debt, dilution, preferred or rollover conversion is assumed anywhere.\n104: [56] A: Glossary\n105:       B: NDA = confidentiality agreement (here, confidentiality and standstill agreements). IOI = indication of interest; LOI = letter of intent. Due diligence = investigation of the target. Formality: documentation/solicitation assessment (Formal/Informal), separate from Conditions level (financing and diligence conditions the bid carries). Round = target-organized solicitation, evaluation or negotiation stage (0 = before the opening; 'post' = outside an identified round). Working date = assigned sort key, not an observed date. Reverse termination fee = fee payable by the buyer side on specified termination (here $15 million). Standstill/sunset = bidder restrictions that lapse to permit proposals. HSR = Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust waiting period. Exclusivity = period of exclusive negotiation. Rollover = shareholder contributing shares into the buyer instead of cashing out.\n106: [57] A: None\n107:       B: Prepared from the supplied filing only. All quotations on the Deal ledger sheet appear verbatim on the Source text sheet; tags in Terms or outcome repeat the structured fields (R1 anchor, Inferred, Bound, Support). Reviewer corrections are expected: see Questions.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/summary_dump.txt, lines 1-107\n1: [1] A: MAC-GRAY / CSC SERVICEWORKS - DEAL LEDGER SUMMARY\n2: [2] A: 1. Status and commercial account\n3: [3] A: AI status\n4:       B: AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction: revision of 19 September 2026 (short form).\n5: [4] A: Source coverage\n6:       B: DEFM14A filed 12/04/2013; work only from this filing and the instruction. Complete Background of the Merger selected and reproduced on the Source text sheet in source order (P-001 to P-088, printed pages 27-41); other filing passages used are X-001 to X-031. Source text is HTML-derived: whitespace normalized, page-break artifacts and repeated 'Table of Contents' headers removed; paragraphs split by printed page breaks appear as separate '(cont.)' rows; no wording changes. Local source filename: raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm.\n7: [5] A: Commercial account\n8:       B: Initiation: after CSC's sale to Pamplona closed in May 2013, Mac-Gray's board explored strategic alternatives, and on June 24, 2013 the Special Committee concluded a sale was in stockholders' best interests and authorized its banker to solicit 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial); Party A had already made an unsolicited $17.00-$19.00 all-cash proposal on June 21, 2013. Competition: four bidder units - Party A (strategic), Party B and Party C (unnamed financial sponsors) and CSC/Pamplona (operating buyer CSC funded by sponsor Pamplona) - were individually recorded among 20 NDA signers and advanced through management meetings and two rounds of revised and final indications, while 16 other signers never submitted. Price path: CSC/Pamplona moved $18.50 (07/23) to $19.50 (09/09) to $20.75 (09/18) and to $21.25 last and best (09/21); Party B peaked at a $21.50-valued package ($19.00 cash plus options) whose cash and certainty lagged; Party A held at $18.00-$19.00 as best and final; Party C stopped at $16.00-$17.00 and did not respond to the final solicitation. Selection: on 09/19 the Special Committee found CSC/Pamplona's proposal most valuable with greater certainty and authorized exclusivity at $21.25; exclusivity was executed 09/24/2013 (to 5 p.m. ET 10/12, extended to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15) with a $15 million reverse termination fee and no financing contingency, Pamplona committed $594 million, and Moab and Mr. MacDonald did not roll over shares. Signing and publicity: the merger agreement was signed 10/14/2013 and announced 10/15/2013; voting agreements covered about 15% of shares; the proxy shows no competing proposal or go-shop and sets the special meeting for 01/08/2014. Observed outcome: signed, not closed - completion expected in the first half of 2014, the HSR waiting period expired 11/27/2013, and a putative class action was filed 11/21/2013.\n9: [6] A: 2. Deal facts\n10: [7] A: Target\n11:       B: Mac-Gray Corporation (Delaware; NYSE-listed; Waltham, Massachusetts), second largest U.S. laundry facilities management contractor. [X-002]\n12: [8] A: Focal acquirer and type\n13:       B: CSC/Pamplona - the acquisition unit of CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. (operating acquirer; the filing calls Party A and CSC/Pamplona its two 'strategic bidders') with equity capital committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P., part of Pamplona Capital Management, which bought CSC in May 2013. Acquisition chain: Parent = Spin Holdco Inc. (wholly owned by CSC); Merger Subsidiary = CSC Fenway, Inc.; Holdings = CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc. Type = Strategic (operating-company acquisition role); sponsor ownership and sponsor financing do not make it Financial, and it is not Mixed. [P-026, P-027, X-001, X-003, X-004, X-005, X-006]\n14: [9] A: Agreed consideration\n15:       B: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest; all-cash; all outstanding shares converted at the effective time; no financing condition. Cash at closing: $21.25 per share. [X-009, X-013, X-030]\n16: [10] A: Signing / announcement / completion\n17:       B: Merger agreement signed 10/14/2013; jointly announced 10/15/2013 before market open; completion expected in the first half of 2014 and NOT observed in the filing (no closed-transaction row). End date 03/31/2014, extendable to 07/31/2014 if only the HSR condition remains. [P-087, P-088, X-016, X-029]\n18: [11] A: Filing identity\n19:       B: DEFM14A, Mac-Gray Corporation, filed 12/04/2013; source file raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm; Background of the Merger at printed pages 27-41; record date 11/27/2013; special meeting 01/08/2014 at 10:00 a.m. Boston. [X-007, X-032]\n20: [12] A: Market benchmarks (dates)\n21:       B: Unaffected reference close $14.72 on 10/11/2013 (last trading day before board approval); 52-week high $15.61 for the period ending 10/11/2013; market close $21.30 on 11/27/2013. Agreed price represents approximately 36% premium to the 52-week high and approximately 44% to the 10/11/2013 close. [X-010, X-011, X-012, X-028]\n22: [13] A: Shares and ownership\n23:       B: 14,758,306 shares outstanding and entitled to vote as of 11/27/2013; voting agreements covered approximately 15% of shares entitled to vote as of that date [X-019]; the related Schedule 13D filed 10/23/2013 reported deemed beneficial ownership of 2,697,484 shares by Parent, Merger Subsidiary, Holdings, CSC, Pamplona and Pamplona Capital Management entities, all disclaimed [X-030]. Moab held approximately 9% in June 2013 [P-019].\n24: [14] A: Financing\n25:       B: $594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. under a commitment letter dated 10/14/2013 for closing funding and related obligations; no financing condition to closing; Pamplona and the Buyer Entities jointly and severally liable for breaches with Pamplona's damages liability capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited). [X-013, X-031]\n26: [15] A: Termination fees\n27:       B: $11 million payable by Mac-Gray (as finally agreed 10/11/2013; earlier proposals were $15 million and $10.5 million); $15 million Parent termination fee. Deal-protection terms are not separate ledger rows per instruction; the fee history appears in the Background (P-074 to P-081). [X-017]\n28: [16] A: Optional labelled calculation\n29:       B: Equity value at the record-date share count = 14,758,306 x $21.25 = formula below (calculation, not a filing assertion; the filing does not state a total equity value, and the termination-fee percentage statements imply larger totals of roughly $341-$350 million on a different share base). No net debt, option, RSU or dilution adjustments are assumed.\n30: [17] A: Equity value (optional; ledger input)\n31:       B: =14758306*21.25\n32: [18] A: None\n33:       B: Sources for inputs: X-007 (shares outstanding) and X-009 (price per share). Excluded from bid-count formulas; flagged as a derived calculation.\n34: [19] A: 3. Process and round map\n35: [20] A: Process map\n36:       B: One sale process (Process 1). Earlier context: the 2011-2012 Discussions were Mac-Gray's prospective acquisition of CSC, not a Mac-Gray sale process (no Process terminated/restarted rows). No separate post-signing stage opened: the proxy discloses no competing proposal, no go-shop and no agreement termination as of 12/04/2013.\n37: [21] A: Round 0 (pre-opening)\n38:       B: No organized round and no Round opened row. Party A contact 04/08/2013 (R003) and unsolicited pre-NDA proposal 06/21/2013 $17.00-$19.00 (R008), standing when round 1 began. Adviser and activist context rows (R001-R007).\n39: [22] A: Round 1 (R009, opens 06/24/2013)\n40:       B: R1 anchor: 06/24/2013 Special Committee decision to consider a sale and authorize solicitation of 50 parties; rejected candidate anchors R008 (06/21 proposal) and R012 (06/28 first NDA); first outreach-wave date not disclosed. Objective: initial outreach and preliminary IOIs. Participants: 50 parties approached (15 strategic, 35 financial); 20 NDA signers entered (R012, R013, R015, R016). Deadline 07/23/2013, treatment Late bids accepted (on-time CSC/Pamplona R018; Party B 07/24 R020; Party C 07/24-25 R021, R023). Finality Not final. Round bidders 4: CSC/Pamplona $18.50, Party B $17.00-$18.00, Party C $15.00-$17.00 (oral), plus Party A's standing $17.00-$19.00 from R008 (explicit inclusion). Ending: 16 residual signers closed as non-submitters (R019); four bidders advanced.\n41: [23] A: Round 2 (R022, opens 07/25/2013)\n42:       B: Objective: staged information access and management meetings, then revised indications. Participants: Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (R023 written IOI; NDA R024). Differential access row R025 (financial bidders broad data-site access; strategic bidders limited, customer data withheld). Deadline set 08/27/2013 for 09/09/2013 (R026); treatment Late bids accepted (CSC/Pamplona and Party B 09/09 R028-R029; Party A and Party C 09/10 R030-R031; reviewed 09/11). Finality Not final. Round bidders 4: CSC/Pamplona $19.50, Party B $18.50, Party A $18.00-$19.00, Party C $16.00-$17.00. Alternative anchor candidate (rejected): R026 (08/27 letter).\n43: [24] A: Round 3 (R033, opens 09/11/2013)\n44:       B: Objective: first request for final indications of interest, with possible short exclusive negotiation. Participants: the same four. Deadline 09/18/2013 (R034), treatment Enforced (target's next step 09/19). Finality Announced as final. Round bidders 3: CSC/Pamplona $20.75 (R035), Party B $21.50-valued package (R037), Party A reaffirmed $18.00-$19.00 best and final (R036); Party C did not submit (R038). Selection 09/19 (R039); final price $21.25 agreed 09/21 (R040).\n45: [25] A: Round 4 (R042, opens 09/24/2013)\n46:       B: Objective: exclusive negotiation and definitive agreement with selected bidder CSC/Pamplona, beginning on execution of the exclusivity agreement (R041). Participants: CSC/Pamplona only; Party A and Party B closed the same day by exclusivity (R043, R044). No bid-submission deadline; exclusivity expiry 5 p.m. ET 10/12/2013 was extended to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15/2013 (R047). Finality Inferred final. Signing R048 (10/14) and announcement R049 (10/15). Alternative treatment (fold into round 3) flagged in Q1.\n47: [26] A: Post-signing\n48:       B: No competing proposal, go-shop start/change or agreement termination is disclosed as of 12/04/2013. Regulatory: HSR filings 10/29/2013, early termination not granted, waiting period expired 11/27/2013 [X-022]. Litigation: putative class action filed 11/21/2013 [X-023]. These belong here, not as ledger rows.\n49: [27] A: 4. Participants and advisers\n50: [28] A: Party A (strategic; unnamed)\n51:       B: First observed 04/08/2013 contact (R003); pre-NDA proposal 06/21/2013 (R008); NDA 08/05/2013 (R024); revised indication 09/10/2013 (R030); best-and-final reaffirmation 09/18/2013 (R036); closed Dropped by target on 09/24/2013 by exclusivity (R043; inferred; exit reason Would not improve earlier offer). Type basis: laundry-industry strategic party, one of the filing's two named strategic bidders [P-034].\n52: [29] A: Party B (financial; unnamed)\n53:       B: First observed NDA 06/28/2013 (R012); IOIs 07/24, 09/09 and the $21.50-valued cash-plus-options proposal 09/18/2013 (R020, R029, R037); closed Dropped by target on 09/24/2013 by exclusivity (R044; inferred; exit reason Terms or process). Type basis: one of the 18 financial bidders, with affiliated-fund equity [P-034, P-052].\n54: [30] A: Party C (financial; unnamed)\n55:       B: First observed NDA 06/30/2013 (R013); oral and written IOIs 07/24-25 (R021, R023) and revised oral indication 09/10/2013 (R031); did not submit at the final-indications solicitation and gave no reasons; closed Did not submit on 09/18/2013 (R038; stated; agency Unknown). Type basis: one of the financial bidders [P-034].\n56: [31] A: CSC/Pamplona (strategic; winner)\n57:       B: First observed contact 06/28/2013 (R011); NDA 07/11/2013 (R015); bids 07/23 $18.50, 09/09 $19.50, 09/18 $20.75 and 09/21 $21.25 last and best (R018, R028, R035, R040); exclusivity 09/24/2013 (R041); signing 10/14/2013 (R048). No exit row (winner). Unit composition: CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. (operating acquirer) and Pamplona (equity capital commitment); Pamplona's funding is support, not a membership change or joint-bidder formation.\n58: [32] A: 16 residual NDA signers (financial)\n59:       B: Entered as residual cohort of 20 signers less the four recorded individually (R016; count 16); closed Did not submit by 07/23/2013 (R019; inferred residual; base assumes all 20 were eligible - flagged Q3).\n60: [33] A: Moab Partners, L.P. (shareholder, approximately 9%)\n61:       B: Not a bidder. Proxy contest and two directors elected 05/30/2013 (R007); rollover request denied 07/06/2013 (R014) and resolved without a rollover by 10/07/2013 (R046); voting agreement at signing (R048).\n62: [34] A: Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. (CEO; significant holder)\n63:       B: Not a bidder. Excluded from sale-process evaluation 06/24/2013 (R009); declined a share rollover 09/11/2013 and wanted a higher value (R032); supportive of $21.25 (R039); voting agreement effective at signing (R048).\n64: [35] A: Advisers\n65:       B: BofA Merrill Lynch (Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner & Smith Incorporated) - Mac-Gray's financial advisor: 2011-2012 Discussions engagement 10/23/2012 (R001), terminated 05/15/2013 (R005), re-engaged for the sale process by Board approval 05/30/2013 with engagement letter 05/31/2013 (R006); delivered the fairness opinion dated 10/14/2013 [X-027]. Goodwin Procter LLP - outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray (observed acting from 05/09/2013, R004; drafted the merger agreement and advised the Special Committee throughout). Kirkland & Ellis LLP - outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona from 09/25/2013 (R042 note). Clients are as stated by the filing; no unclear client affiliations identified.\n66: [36] A: 5. Counts and auction screen\n67: [37] A: NDA signers (ledger)\n68:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"NDA signed\")\n69: [38] A: None\n70:       B: Filing assertion: 20 (two strategic bidders - Party A and CSC/Pamplona - and 18 financial bidders, including Party B and Party C) [P-034]. Ledger = 4 individually recorded signers + 16 residual cohort = 20; reconciles exactly. Residual dates and eligibility are uncertain (Q3).\n71: [39] A: First sale-related contacts (ledger)\n72:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Contact\")\n73: [40] A: None\n74:       B: Filing process-level assertion: 50 parties approached (15 strategic, 35 financial) [P-032, P-033]. Only Party A (04/08/2013) and CSC/Pamplona (06/28/2013) are individually dated; the other contacts are not individually reported, so no exact reconciliation is claimed.\n75: [41] A: Round-1 round bidders (submissions)\n76:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,1,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,1,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid reaffirmed\")\n77: [42] A: None\n78:       B: Explicit inclusion: + 1 standing round-0 proposal (Party A, R008, whose Bid row sits in round 0 but who participated in round 1) = 4 round bidders. Units, not submissions or unique firms.\n79: [43] A: Round-2 round bidders\n80:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,2,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,2,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid reaffirmed\")\n81: [44] A: None\n82:       B: Four units: CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party A, Party C. Not a submission count (Party C has two rows in round 1 and one in round 2; revisions carry Count 0).\n83: [45] A: Round-3 round bidders\n84:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,3,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$F:$F,3,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Bid reaffirmed\")\n85: [46] A: None\n86:       B: Three units (CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party A); Party C did not submit and is an outcome row (R038), not a round bidder. Round 4 has no bid rows: one unit continued in exclusive definitive negotiation.\n87: [47] A: Outcome tallies (affected units)\n88:       B: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,'Deal ledger'!$P:$P,\"Yes\",'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Dropped by target\")\n89: [48] A: None\n90:       B: Dropped by target = 2 units (Party A, Party B at 09/24). Did not submit: 16 residual at 07/23 (R019) + Party C at 09/18 (R038) = 17 units; formula above shows only the Dropped tally; totals are occurrences/affected units, not unique permanent exits. Winner CSC/Pamplona has no exit row.\n91: [49] A: Auction screen\n92:       B: Met: more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process - four units are individually recorded (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) among 20 signers total. Excluded: no lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements reported; no agreements expressly reused from an earlier attempt (the 2011-2012 Discussions produced no reused NDA).\n93: [50] A: Per-stage balance (participants)\n94:       B: R0: entrants 1 (Party A) - exits 0 = 1 live. R1: entrants +19 (16 cohort + Party B + Party C + CSC/Pamplona; Party A already in) = 20; exits -16 (residual non-submitters, R019) = 4. R2: exits 0 = 4. R3: exits -1 (Party C, R038) = 3. R4: exits -2 (Party A and Party B by exclusivity, R043-R044) = 1 = winner at signing (R048); no participant left open. Inferred share of exits: 18 of 19 (the 16 residual plus the two exclusivity drops); Party C's exit is stated. Counts are tally contributions, not population balances.\n95: [51] A: 6. Comparability and inputs\n96: [52] A: Other-scope proposals\n97:       B: None: every recorded proposal concerns acquisition of the whole company's equity. No segment, asset, minority or other-scope bids and no group price envelopes.\n98: [53] A: Unusual consideration\n99:       B: Party B's 09/18/2013 cash-plus-options package: $19.00 cash at closing plus options it valued at $2.50 per share (10% of new equity, strike at its initial cost basis, vesting over five years on base-case projections). Recorded as All cash = No; structured price cells show the cash component and the bidder's stated total ($19.00-$21.50) and are flagged as a package representation (Q7). No CVR or earnout in the signed deal.\n100: [54] A: Currency and units\n101:       B: All amounts USD per share; no currency conversion performed. Agreed consideration and all recorded bid prices are per share of Mac-Gray common stock.\n102: [55] A: Stated deal inputs\n103:       B: Shares outstanding 14,758,306 at 11/27/2013 [X-007]; market close $21.30 on 11/27/2013 [X-012]; unaffected close $14.72 and 52-week high $15.61 on 10/11/2013 [X-010, X-011, X-027]; $594 million Pamplona commitment [X-013, X-031]; $11 million / $15 million termination fees [X-017]; voting agreements approximately 15% [X-019, X-030]. No net debt, dilution, preferred or rollover conversion is assumed anywhere.\n104: [56] A: Glossary\n105:       B: NDA = confidentiality agreement (here, confidentiality and standstill agreements). IOI = indication of interest; LOI = letter of intent. Due diligence = investigation of the target. Formality: documentation/solicitation assessment (Formal/Informal), separate from Conditions level (financing and diligence conditions the bid carries). Round = target-organized solicitation, evaluation or negotiation stage (0 = before the opening; 'post' = outside an identified round). Working date = assigned sort key, not an observed date. Reverse termination fee = fee payable by the buyer side on specified termination (here $15 million). Standstill/sunset = bidder restrictions that lapse to permit proposals. HSR = Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust waiting period. Exclusivity = period of exclusive negotiation. Rollover = shareholder contributing shares into the buyer instead of cashing out.\n106: [57] A: None\n107:       B: Prepared from the supplied filing only. All quotations on the Deal ledger sheet appear verbatim on the Source text sheet; tags in Terms or outcome repeat the structured fields (R1 anchor, Inferred, Bound, Support). Reviewer corrections are expected: see Questions."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/summary_dump.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825220470,"end":1789825220558}}}}
