{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825262684,"sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e620f800190MdCjjaWIdqeo","sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","messageID":"msg_0b9e5f746001RDyVsKaLi4KVEC","type":"tool","id":"call_00_S3SdZ8H8h1abyZ6VTnrw8923","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF' > /tmp/opencode/questions_dump.txt\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\nq = wb['Questions']\nfor r in range(2, q.max_row+1):\n    print(f\"===== {q.cell(row=r,column=1).value} | {q.cell(row=r,column=2).value} =====\")\n    print(\"RECOMMENDED:\", q.cell(row=r,column=3).value)\n    print(\"WHY:\", q.cell(row=r,column=4).value)\n    print(\"AFFECTED:\", q.cell(row=r,column=5).value)\n    print(\"CONSEQUENCE:\", q.cell(row=r,column=6).value)\n    print(\"STATUS:\", q.cell(row=r,column=7).value)\n    print()\nEOF\nhead -60 /tmp/opencode/questions_dump.txt"},"output":"===== Q1 | Process and round map; inferred starts; rejected boundary candidates =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep one process and the four rounds as built: R1 06/24/2013 (sale decision/50-party solicitation; rejected anchors R008 and R012); R2 07/25/2013 (staged access and revised-IOI stage; rejected alternative R026, the 08/27/2013 letter); R3 09/11/2013 (first final-indications request; Announced as final); R4 09/24/2013 (executed exclusivity and definitive negotiation; Inferred final; alternative = fold into R3). Treat the 2011-2012 Discussions as context, not a second process.\nWHY: Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R022 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders'); the 08/27 letter only communicated the deadline. R3 is the target's first request for final indications (R033 quote). R4 applies the 'moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders' trigger; exclusivity inside an already-established final negotiation stage would not open a round. Sources: P-021 (R009), P-038/P-039 (R022), P-056 (R033), P-068 (R041-R042).\nAFFECTED: R008, R009, R012, R022, R026, R033, R040, R041, R042; rounds/finality fields on R009/R022/R033/R042\nCONSEQUENCE: Dating R2 at 08/27 moves the start of the staged-access stage and its access row (R025); merging R4 into R3 would put exclusivity, the two closures and signing in R3 and delete the Inferred-final row; treating R1 as opening at the 06/21 proposal would pull Party A's bid out of round 0.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q2 | Deadline changes and elapsed-deadline treatments =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep: 07/23/2013 Late bids accepted; 09/09/2013 Late bids accepted; 09/18/2013 Enforced. No bid deadline was revised; the 10/12/2013 exclusivity expiry was extended (recorded on R047, not as a bid Deadline row).\nWHY: 07/23: Party B (07/24) and Party C (07/24-25) were considered by the Special Committee on 07/25 without revision. 09/09: Party A and Party C submitted 09/10 and were reviewed 09/11 without extension; the target itself later solicited CSC/Pamplona's 09/21 price revision, which belongs to continuing negotiation and is not late acceptance. 09/18: the next step was selection (09/19), so Enforced. Sources: P-026, P-035 to P-037 (Late bids); P-052 to P-055 (09/09); P-059 to P-062 (09/18 selection); P-078, P-079, P-082 (extension).\nAFFECTED: R010, R017, R019, R026, R027, R034, R044, R047; Deadline treatment and Due date fields\nCONSEQUENCE: Re-labelling 07/23 or 09/09 as Enforced, or 09/18 as Unclear, changes the term the target applied to its stage and implies (unsupported) formal revision or inaction.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q3 | Inferred residual rows and NDA population uncertainty =====\nRECOMMENDED: Retain the 16-person residual for the NDA cohort (R016) and for the 07/23 non-submission (R019), base = 20 signers. Keep the caveat that only the four individually dated signers are certain; all eligibility arithmetic uses the filing's stated totals.\nWHY: Base and split: P-026 ('a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders'). Accounting at the first transition: P-037 names only Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona and Party A's standing proposal. Arithmetic: 20 - 4 = 16. Uncertainty: the 16 signers' dates are unstated and signers whose NDAs postdate 07/23 would reduce the residual; Party A signed only on 08/05 but is shown continuing, so it is not in the residual.\nAFFECTED: R012, R013, R015, R016, R019, R020, R021, R022, R024; Count/Dates fields on R016 and R019\nCONSEQUENCE: Changing the base or the accounted-for set changes both inferred Counts and the per-stage balance; adding individual rows for anonymous members would invent identities.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q4 | Participation outcomes and agency (including every inferred closing row) =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep: Party A and Party B Dropped by target on 09/24/2013 (Inferred: exclusivity; Decided by Target; reasons Would not improve earlier offer and Terms or process); Party C Did not submit on 09/18/2013 (stated; Decided by Unknown; Not stated); winner no exit row. No participant left open.\nWHY: Exclusivity was executed 09/24/2013 with CSC/Pamplona with no notice to Party A or Party B reported (P-068; Party A's last act P-059). Party C's non-submission and absence of reasons are stated in P-059/P-060; the filing reports no notice or discouragement, so agency is left Unknown. Convention: every participant that entered is closed once.\nAFFECTED: R019, R038, R043, R044; Decided by / Exit reason / Outcome basis fields\nCONSEQUENCE: Assigning withdrawals or bidder agency without notice evidence would misstate participation; failing to close A and B would break the per-stage balance at signing.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q5 | Formality of the final-stage indications (borderline Formal calls) =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep Formal for the 09/18/2013 responses (CSC/Pamplona $20.75; Party B $21.50 package) and for Party A's best-and-final reaffirmation, carried to CSC/Pamplona's 09/21/2013 last-and-best. Alternative for Party A: Informal if a phone reiteration is judged not to be a response on the requested written basis. Earlier IOIs remain Informal.\nWHY: Formality signal 2: 'a response on the requested basis to a genuine final, binding or best-and-final solicitation'; a non-binding IOI can be Formal; no retrospective upgrading of earlier offers. Sources: P-059 (09/18 responses), P-056 (final request), P-063 (09/21 confirmation). Party A's call is the borderline case and is flagged here rather than upgraded silently.\nAFFECTED: R035, R036, R037, R040; Formality fields; context rows R008, R018, R020, R021, R023, R028-R031\nCONSEQUENCE: Downgrading Party A changes only its row label (its exit basis is unaffected); upgrading earlier IOIs would contradict the no-retrospective-upgrade rule.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q6 | Conditions levels that turn on diligence or financing statements =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep Heavy for pre-substantive-diligence IOIs (R008, R018, R020, R021, R023) and for Party B's later bids (R029, R037 - reported absence of a firm financing commitment). Keep Light for CSC/Pamplona's 09/09 and later bids (R028, R035, R040 - committed sponsor financing, no stated diligence condition). Keep Insufficient evidence for Party C's 09/10/2013 revised indication (R031 - price only, financing silence).\nWHY: Heavy-by-context applies to preliminary indications made before data-room or management access; 'less conditional' comparisons were not converted into absolute levels; silence neither raises nor lowers a level. Sources: P-026, P-035 to P-037 (pre-DD IOIs), P-052 (CSC/Pamplona committed funding; Party B no firm commitment), P-053 (Party C silence), P-047 (access staging).\nAFFECTED: R008, R018, R020, R021, R023, R028-R031, R035-R037, R040; Conditions level and Conditions detail fields\nCONSEQUENCE: Reassigning a level changes the comparable conditionality of final offers and the four documented Heavy-by-context calls at the first stage.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q7 | Price representation for Party B's cash-plus-options package and related conventions =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep Price low 19.00 / Price high 21.50 with Price kind Bidder range, All cash No and Cash at closing 19.00, with Terms stating that the cells show the cash component and the bidder's stated total valuation - a package, not a submitted range. Alternative: blank the structured price cells and keep the package only in Terms.\nWHY: The filing gives $19.00 cash at closing plus options valued at $2.50 (total $21.50) (P-059); the instruction directs that package values be attributed, not treated as guaranteed cash, and that the contingent part stay in Terms. Sources: P-059, P-062 (Special Committee risk view).\nAFFECTED: R037; Price low/high/kind/origin, All cash, Cash at closing fields; comparability note in Summary section 6\nCONSEQUENCE: Blank cells reduce structured comparability but avoid any reading of $21.50 as cash; leaving as recorded preserves the bidder's own valuation with an explicit flag.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n===== Q8 | Date conventions and record-keeping items =====\nRECOMMENDED: Accept the assigned Working dates and their methods: residual NDA midpoint 07/17/2013 (R016); 07/23/2013 deadline-set row by sequence (R010); Moab resolution bounded to 10/07/2013 (R046); inferred closures assigned to deadline/decision days (R019, R038, R043, R044). Accept the preserved source typo 'July 27, 2103' with the proposed correction to 2013 (R024), and the structural choices: one row each for the Moab and MacDonald rollover relationships, adviser rows for BofA (old and new mandates) and Goodwin Procter service, and no rows for termination/reverse fees, liability caps, voting agreements, post-signing covenants or successive drafts (folded into R040, R041, R047, R048).\nWHY: All are instruction conventions (sections 5.4, 8.1, 10.2) or explicit materiality exclusions (section 4); quotations on the Source text sheet preserve wording and qualification, and no working date falls outside its Date from/Date to or contradicts the filing's before/after bounds.\nAFFECTED: R001, R005, R006, R010, R014, R016, R019, R024, R032, R038, R043, R044, R046, R047, R048; Date from/to, Working date, Date basis, Date method, Page fields\nCONSEQUENCE: Changing conventions reorders display or shifts assigned dates but not the underlying facts; moving the typo correction or rollover rows would affect only those rows' framing.\nSTATUS: Pending\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"===== Q1 | Process and round map; inferred starts; rejected boundary candidates =====\nRECOMMENDED: Keep one process and the four rounds as built: R1 06/24/2013 (sale decision/50-party solicitation; rejected anchors R008 and R012); R2 07/25/2013 (staged access and revised-IOI stage; rejected alternative R026, the 08/27/2013 letter); R3 09/11/2013 (first final-indications request; Announced as final); R4 09/24/2013 (executed exclusivity and definitive negotiation; Inferred final; alternative = fold into R3). Treat the 2011-2012 Discussions as context, not a second process.\nWHY: Anchors follow the instruction's opening rules: R1 uses the launching decision because the first outreach wave is undated (outreach executed within days; first NDA 06/28). R2 uses the selection of advancing participants plus a stage-linked offer request (authorization R022 quote: 'authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders')