{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825297889,"sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e68c370015NeZyWXMpu8ex7_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f462b3faeffehKvke01c5BeJ5s","messageID":"msg_0b9e68c370015NeZyWXMpu8ex7","type":"text","text":"**Deliverable:** `/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx` — 49-row deal ledger, with **Deal ledger / Summary / Questions / Source text** visible and **Lists** hidden. Every quotation in the ledger was verified to appear verbatim on the Source text sheet (all 88 background rows, pages 27–41, plus 32 used passages), internal links, dropdowns, outline groups, and formula totals were checked programmatically.\n\n**Plain account of the sale.** After CSC was sold to Pamplona in May 2013, Mac-Gray's board explored strategic alternatives; on 06/24/2013 the Special Committee concluded a sale was best for stockholders and had BofA Merrill Lynch solicit 50 parties. Party A had already proposed $17–$19 in cash on 06/21/2013. Four bidders — Party A (strategic), unnamed financial sponsors Party B and Party C, and strategic CSC/Pamplona (CSC, funded by Pamplona) — emerged from 20 confidentiality signers and advanced through management meetings and two rounds of revised/final indications. CSC/Pamplona led the price path $18.50 → $19.50 → $20.75 → $21.25 (last and best); Party B peaked at a $21.50-valued cash-plus-options package; Party A held at $18–$19 as best and final; Party C stopped bidding and did not respond to the final solicitation. On 09/19 the Special Committee selected CSC/Pamplona and, after exclusivity (09/24, extended to 10/15) and definitive negotiations, the merger agreement was signed 10/14 and announced 10/15/2013 for $21.25 per share in cash, with $594M of Pamplona financing, no financing condition, and $11M/$15M termination fees. **Observed outcome: signed, not closed** — completion was expected in 1H 2014; the HSR waiting period expired 11/27/2013 and a putative class action was filed 11/21/2013.\n\n**Most consequential review items (recommendations in the Questions sheet):**\n- **Q1 – Round map:** keep one process and four rounds (R1 06/24 outreach; R2 07/25 staged access/revised IOIs; R3 09/11 final indications; R4 09/24 exclusivity/definitives), with the R3/R4 split flagged as the main boundary judgment.\n- **Q2 – Deadlines:** 07/23 and 09/09 *Late bids accepted*; 09/18 *Enforced*; exclusivity expiry extended (not a bid deadline).\n- **Q3/Q4 – Inferred rows:** the 16-signer residual (NDA cohort and 07/23 non-submission) and the 09/24 exclusivity closures of Party A and Party B; confirm the eligibility-base caveat for the residual.\n- **Q5/Q6 – Formality and conditions:** final-stage IOIs treated as Formal (signal 2), including Party A's borderline oral best-and-final; Heavy by context for pre-diligence IOIs and Party B's uncommitted financing; Party C 09/10 left *Insufficient evidence*.\n- **Q7 – Party B price representation:** price cells 19.00/21.50 flagged as a cash-plus-options package (not a range); alternative is blank structured cells.\n- **Q8 – Conventions:** assigned working dates, the preserved source typo \"July 27, 2103\", and the decision to keep fee/voting-agreement/draft negotiation out of rows (folded into the bid, decision and signing rows).\n\n**What I could not verify / unsupported features.** This environment could not open the workbook visually (LibreOffice crashes here) and has no Excel, so rendering of the collapsed outline groups, dropdown arrows and auto row heights is unverified — I validated them structurally instead (15 list validations, 49 resolving internal hyperlinks, hidden Lists sheet, outline levels, unique IDs, non-decreasing working dates). Formula cells contain live formulas plus injected cached totals, and the workbook is set to recalculate on open; the optional equity-value arithmetic is labelled as a calculation, not a filing statement. This is an AI first pass and has not been human-reviewed; Party A/B/C are unnamed in the filing and no outside identities were used.","time":{"start":1789825289278,"end":1789825297889}}}
